E["item:corrupted-brain-stem"] = {t="item",n="Corrupted Brain Stem",z="blackfathom",s="In Blackfathom Deeps and along Ashenvale's coast, Corrupted Brain Stem specimens come from twisted naga and satyrs. Gershala Nightwhisper of Auberdine studies the deformities caused by reckless magic. Night elf scholars hope the findings can help keep the blood elves from suffering the same fate.",h="In Blackfathom Deeps and along Ashenvale's coast, Corrupted Brain Stem specimens come from twisted naga and...",sec={{t="Anatomy of Transformation",b="Naga and satyrs bear the marks of forbidden magic and demonic pacts. Long ago, reckless kaldorei highborne became serpent-like aquatic beasts and demonic horned fiends. Their brain stems show heavy physical mutation, proof of how deeply corruptive energies altered the nervous systems of beings who were once elves.",sp=0},{t="Gershala's Warning",b="Gershala Nightwhisper watches troubling rumors about the blood elves of the Eastern Kingdoms from Auberdine. He fears their use of demonic sorcery will create another generation of monsters on Azeroth, so he sends adventurers into Blackfathom Deeps. By examining naga and satyr tissues, he hopes to trace magical degeneration before another elven culture is lost.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures yield a Corrupted Brain Stem?",a="Naga and satyrs in Blackfathom Deeps and along the Ashenvale coast yield them, including Blackfathom oracles, sea witches, and Fallenroot satyrs.",al={"who drops brain stems","corrupted brain stem drop","where to get brain stems"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who wants these brain stems and why?",a="Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine wants the stems for anatomical research into magical corruption.",al={"who needs corrupted brain stem","gershala quest","turn in brain stems"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are night elves hoping to learn from these specimens?",a="Night elves hope to learn how demonic energies alter elven biology. Gershala fears the blood elves may become monsters, as the ancient highborne became naga and satyrs.",al={"why study naga satyr","researching the corruption lore","blood elf connection"},it="purpose"},{q="Can these be found outside of the Blackfathom Deeps caverns?",a="Yes. Some Fallenroot satyrs and Blackfathom tide priestesses outside the cavern entrance along the Ashenvale coast carry them.",al={"outside blackfathom","ashenvale brain stems","do surface mobs drop them"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a Corrupted Brain Stem?",a="A Corrupted Brain Stem is an anatomical specimen harvested from the satyrs and naga dwelling within and around Blackfathom Deeps. Both races were once night elves whose bodies and minds were violently altered by demonic pacts or ancient, shadowy depths. These brain stems carry the physical hallmarks of that magical deformation, making them valuable anatomical subjects for scholars studying how dark sorcery twists mortal flesh.",al={"what is corrupted brain stem","corrupted brain stem item","corrupted brainstem lore"},it="identity",add="3ff1da04"},{q="Where does a Corrupted Brain Stem come from?",a="These brain stems are taken from the Fallenroot satyrs and Blackfathom naga inhabiting the subterranean grottos and ruins around Blackfathom Deeps along the Ashenvale coast. Rather than being manufactured items, they are biological remnants of creatures warped over millennia by corruption, fel power, and dark transformations.",al={"where do corrupted brain stems come from","who drops corrupted brain stem","corrupted brain stem origin"},it="origin",add="53f0c38a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, these remains recall their people's tragic history and the monstrous effects of unchecked arcane and fel meddling.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance scout in Ashenvale, you brave Blackfathom's depths to help Auberdine's scholars understand growing threats across Azeroth."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","blackfathom deeps","corrupted brain stem","gershala nightwhisper","naga","researching the corruption","satyr"},rel={"quest:1275","npc:gershala-nightwhisper","zone:blackfathom","zone:ashenvale","subzone:auberdine","npc:lady-sarevess","topic:naga","topic:satyr"},src={"Corrupted Brain Stem","Researching the Corruption (Classic)"}}
E["item:fathom-core"] = {t="item",n="Fathom Core",z="blackfathom",s="Beneath the Moonshrine Ruins, the Fathom Core records the elements at work in Blackfathom Deeps. The Earthen Ring seeks it to learn how the Twilight's Hammer is manipulating those forces.",h="Beneath the Moonshrine Ruins, the Fathom Core records the elements at work in Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Elemental Chronicle",b="The Fathom Core rests inside an ancient fathom stone beneath the Moonshrine Ruins. It records shifts, disruptions, and surges in the elements over time. Je'neu Sancrea, an Earthen Ring shaman at Zoram'gar Outpost, seeks the core to understand how the Twilight's Hammer cultists are turning the region's elements to their own ends.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Fathom Core?",a="The Fathom Core records a detailed history of elemental activity nearby. It rests inside an ancient fathom stone in the Moonshrine Ruins.",al={"what does fathom core do","fathom core lore","what is it"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Fathom Core located?",a="The Fathom Core lies deep in Blackfathom Deeps, beneath the Ashenvale coast. It rests inside a fathom stone under the waters of the Moonshrine Ruins.",al={"fathom core location","where to find fathom core","fathom stone location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the Fathom Core and why?",a="Je'neu Sancrea, an Earthen Ring shaman at Zoram'gar Outpost, seeks the Fathom Core. He and his circle hope its record of elemental shifts will help them understand and counter the Twilight's Hammer's activities in the ruins.",al={"who needs fathom core","why does je'neu want fathom core","earthen ring fathom core"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer interested in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cultists have taken up residence in the submerged ruins to coerce and corrupt the local elements. They seek to bend those forces to dark purposes and claim control of the subterranean temple.",al={"twilight's hammer blackfathom","cultists in bfd"},it="motive"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see why the Earthen Ring values the Fathom Core: its record can reveal how others manipulate the elements.",["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the Fathom Core aids Je'neu Sancrea and helps secure the Horde's foothold at Zoram'gar Outpost against the Twilight's Hammer's corruptive designs."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","fathom core","fathom stone","je'neu sancrea","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"quest:6921","npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},src={"Fathom Core","Amongst the Ruins (Classic)"}}
E["item:head-of-kelris"] = {t="item",n="Head of Kelris",z="blackfathom",s="Agents of the Argent Dawn seek Kelris's severed head to confirm his fall and the end of his sacrifices.",h="Agents of the Argent Dawn seek Kelris's severed head to confirm his fall and the end of his sacrifices.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Ruin",b="In Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight Lord Kelris led sacrifices to Aku'mai, a monstrous servant of an Old God. Taking his head marks the end of his rule over the Twilight's Hammer cultists and their naga allies in the cavern. The head must reach the surface so leaders can know his bloody ceremonies have ended.",sp=0},{t="Proof for the Dawn",b="The Argent Dawn had presumed Kelris dead or lost for months before his influence returned with Kalimdor's encroaching shadows. His head, brought to agents in Darnassus or Thunder Bluff, settles lingering bounties and confirms that his attempt to plunge the world into primeval chaos has been stopped.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Twilight Lord Kelris?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris led the Twilight's Hammer sect in Blackfathom Deeps. Allied with the naga, he sacrificed innocents to Aku'mai, a hydra servant of an Old God, seeking dark power and ancient chaos.",al={"who is kelris","kelris lore","twilight lord kelris"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the Head of Kelris?",a="Alliance champions take the head to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus. Horde adventurers bring it to Bashana Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Selgorm serves the Argent Dawn, while Bashana belongs to the Cenarion Circle.",al={"who takes kelris head","head of kelris turn in","who do i give kelris head to"},it="wants"},{q="Why does the Argent Dawn care about Kelris?",a="The Argent Dawn tracks threats to Azeroth. Kelris had long eluded them, and his Old God worship and sacrifices of innocents threatened Kalimdor's balance.",al={"why argent dawn kelris","argent dawn blackfathom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the head obtained?",a="The head comes from Twilight Lord Kelris's corpse in his sanctum within Blackfathom Deeps, beneath the Zoram Strand on Ashenvale's coast.",al={"where to get kelris head","kelris head location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What is the Head of Kelris?",a="It is the severed head of Twilight Lord Kelris, the leader of the Twilight's Hammer cultists who took root deep within the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. It serves as gruesome, undeniable proof that the cult's sinister master in the sunken temple has been slain and his rituals brought to an end.",al={"head of kelris","what is head of kelris","kelris head item"},it="identity",add="c257c517"},{q="Where does the Head of Kelris come from?",a="The head is taken directly from Twilight Lord Kelris in the depths of Blackfathom Deeps along the Zoram Strand. You must fight your way past his fanatical cultists and aberrant servants to slay the twilight lord in his inner sanctum before claiming it.",al={"where to get head of kelris","head of kelris origin","how to get head of kelris"},it="origin",add="0e645b89"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you take Kelris's head to Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus, avenging the desecration of an ancient night elf temple dedicated to Elune.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer, you present the head to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff, earning the Cenarion Circle's trust and proving your dedication to cleansing Kalimdor's corruption."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","bashana runetotem","blackfathom deeps","blackfathom villainy","head of kelris","selgorm","twilight lord kelris"},rel={"npc:twilight-lord-kelris","quest:1200","zone:blackfathom","npc:aku-mai","topic:argent-dawn","npc:dawnwatcher-selgorm","npc:bashana-runetotem","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Head of Kelris","Blackfathom Villainy (Alliance)","Blackfathom Villainy (Horde)"}}
E["item:lorgalis-manuscript"] = {t="item",n="Lorgalis Manuscript",z="blackfathom",s="The Lorgalis Manuscript lies hidden beneath Ashenvale in the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. The ancient text concerns the Old Gods, and dark scholars covet its words about powers that sleep.",h="The Lorgalis Manuscript lies hidden beneath Ashenvale in the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Tome of Those Who Sleep",b="The Lorgalis Manuscript lies at the bottom of Blackfathom Deeps, where long-dead elves once lived before their city fell. Lorgalis wrote of the Old Gods, who raged across Azeroth when the world was new and now lie chained and sleeping. The text praises Aku'mai, a servant of the Old Gods who dwells in the Deeps. Its lore is said to open mystical doorways and stir ancient beings sleeping deep beneath the world. The manuscript rests in a pitted iron chest among the flooded corridors, drawing the attention of cultists and shadow scholars alike.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="In Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, the eccentric collector Gerrig Bonegrip hires adventurers to cross the sea and retrieve the text. Bonegrip speaks with reverence of the end days and the awakening of sleeping deities. He intends to have the manuscript transcribed and shared among his shadowy circle of brothers and sisters, spreading forbidden knowledge that surface folk were never meant to understand.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Lorgalis Manuscript?",a="The Lorgalis Manuscript is an old text written by Lorgalis about the Old Gods. Its contents are said to reveal how to open doorways and awaken slumbering primordial beings.",al={"what is lorgalis manuscript","lorgalis book lore","what does the manuscript do"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the manuscript located?",a="The manuscript rests in a pitted iron chest deep within Blackfathom Deeps, a ruined night elven temple along the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale.",al={"where to find lorgalis manuscript","manuscript location","blackfathom chest"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants the manuscript?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip, who works from the Forlorn Cavern in Ironforge, wants the manuscript recovered. He plans to copy it and share its teachings with his secretive peers.",al={"who wants lorgalis manuscript","gerrig bonegrip quest","who is bonegrip"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Gerrig Bonegrip talk about the end days?",a="Bonegrip reveres and studies the Old Gods. He seeks ancient elven writings about awakening Those Who Sleep, which he believes heralds the coming end times.",al={"gerrig end days","bonegrip cultist","bonegrip old gods"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the Lorgalis Manuscript come from, and who made it?",a="The manuscript was written by one Lorgalis and lies at the bottom of Blackfathom Deeps, the sunken ruins where long-dead elves once dwelt before their city fell. Who Lorgalis was is not recorded. The text sets down forbidden lore about the Old Gods and Those Who Sleep and praises Aku'mai, a servant of the Old Gods who dwells in the Deeps. It rests locked in a pitted iron chest in the flooded halls.",al={"lorgalis manuscript origin","who wrote lorgalis manuscript","where was lorgalis manuscript made"},it="origin",add="61ae2bf7"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a Warlock, the manuscript offers a rare glimpse into forbidden lore about the Old Gods and the entities of the deep, knowledge coveted by those who practice dark arts.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you find the text in drowned ruins where your people once lived. Its reverence for Aku'mai and the Old Gods reveals the dark worship rooted in those fallen halls."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","forlorn cavern","gerrig bonegrip","ironforge","lorgalis","manuscript","old god","those who sleep"},rel={"quest:971","npc:gerrig-bonegrip","zone:blackfathom","subzone:forlorn-cavern","zone:ashenvale","zone:ironforge","topic:old-god"},src={"Lorgalis Manuscript","Knowledge in the Deeps (Classic)"}}
E["item:sapphire-of-aku-mai"] = {t="item",n="Sapphire of Aku'Mai",z="blackfathom",s="Along Blackfathom Deeps, the naga are harvesting the glowing Sapphires of Aku'Mai. Water spirits cling to the crystals, and Je'neu Sancrea seeks help confiscating them before their arcane power can be exploited.",h="Along Blackfathom Deeps, the naga are harvesting the glowing Sapphires of Aku'Mai.",sec={{t="Gems of the Deep",b="Blackfathom Deeps holds Sapphires of Aku'Mai in its watery cavern entrances along Ashenvale's Zoram Strand. Water spirits cling to the crystalline formations, rich in elemental energy, making them potent aids in magical workings. When scouts reported the subterranean naga quarrying the gems from cavern walls, Je'neu Sancrea, a shaman, sought adventuring help to confiscate them. In naga hands, the stones could fuel devastating arcane rites.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Sapphire of Aku'Mai?",a="Sapphires of Aku'Mai are vibrant crystals lining the walls of Blackfathom Deeps. Water spirits cling to them, giving the gems deep arcane and elemental resonance.",al={"what is this crystal","sapphire of aku'mai lore","what are these gems"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the naga collecting these sapphires?",a="Je'neu Sancrea suspects the naga intend to harness the crystals' water and arcane energies for dangerous sorcery in the submerged temple, though their exact intentions are uncertain.",al={"why do naga want sapphires","naga crystal harvesting"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is looking for these sapphires?",a="Je'neu Sancrea, an Earthen Ring shaman at Zoram'gar Outpost on Ashenvale's Zoram Strand, asks travelers to gather the sapphires and keep them from naga hands.",al={"who wants sapphires of akumai","who turns in essence of akumai"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are these crystals directly tied to the beast Aku'mai?",a="The crystals take their name from Aku'mai, the monstrous hydra in the deeps, but grow naturally in the cavern walls. Their name reflects their nearness to the dark presence in the ruins.",al={"aku'mai connection","is it from akumai"},it="ties"},{q="Where do the Sapphires of Aku'Mai come from, and who made them?",a="These large sapphire clusters grow naturally along the cavern walls within the beginning tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps. They are not crafted by mortal hands; rather, they are natural mineral formations steeped in the cavern's ambient energies. Water spirits naturally cling to the crystals, granting them inherent elemental potency.",al={"origin of sapphire of aku'mai","who made sapphire of akumai","where do sapphires of aku'mai come from"},it="origin",add="12f03799"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As an Earthen Ring shaman, you can sense the water spirits bound within these gems and see the naga harvest as a threat to the elements.",["class:Mage"]="The sapphires' natural saturation with water makes them valued conduits for potent arcane components."},kw={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","crystals","je'neu sancrea","naga","sapphire","water spirits","zoram strand"},rel={"quest:6563","npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","npc:aku-mai","topic:naga","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:6562","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Sapphire of Aku'Mai","The Essence of Aku'Mai (Classic)"}}
E["item:twilight-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Twilight Pendant",z="blackfathom",s="In Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight Pendants mark the cultists who serve the Twilight's Hammer. The Argent Dawn seeks them as proof of the cult's work along Ashenvale's coast.",h="In Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight Pendants mark the cultists who serve the Twilight's Hammer.",sec={{t="Tokens of the Old Gods",b="Beneath the drowned ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, the Twilight's Hammer gathers with the naga to honor the chaotic Old Gods. Shadowmages, aquamancers, reavers, and loreseekers all wear Twilight Pendants as signs of devotion to their shadowy patrons. The cult keeps to the ruins of the former night elf temple, so these pendants offer outsiders one of the few ways to learn how many cultists gather there and hinder their plans.",sp=0},{t="The Argent Dawn's Vigils",b="Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus seeks Twilight Pendants as evidence that the growing darkness is being driven back. Blackfathom Deeps once held a pristine moonwell, and its desecration by void-worshipers threatens Kalimdor. Gathering the pendants shows that the Twilight's Hammer foothold in Ashenvale is being dismantled before its patrons can unleash greater terror.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Twilight Pendant?",a="Twilight Pendants are identifying amulets worn by the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. They show the cultists' devotion to the Old Gods and their rites.",al={"twilight pendant info","what are twilight pendants"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Argent Guard Manados want these pendants?",a="Argent Guard Manados seeks Twilight Pendants in Darnassus as proof that the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps is being struck down before its plans can mature.",al={"who wants twilight pendant","why collect twilight pendants"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who wears these pendants?",a="Twilight Acolytes, Aquamancers, Shadowmages, Loreseekers, Elementalists, and Reavers wear these pendants inside Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"who drops twilight pendant","where do twilight pendants come from"},it="people"},{q="What threat does the Twilight's Hammer pose in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Twilight's Hammer allies with the naga to revive worship of the Old Gods. Its rites desecrate an ancient night elf moonwell and could spread terror across Kalimdor.",al={"what is twilights hammer doing in bfd","why are cultists in ashenvale"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know Blackfathom Deeps once held a revered and powerful moonwell. Reclaiming its symbols of corruption is a matter of deep sanctity for the kaldorei.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can bring these trophies to Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus. They show the Alliance's support for the Argent Dawn's campaign against hidden evils in northern Kalimdor."},kw={"argent guard manados","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","old gods","twilight falls","twilight pendant","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:1199","npc:argent-guard-manados","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:argent-dawn","topic:old-god","zone:ashenvale","zone:darnassus"},src={"Twilight Pendant","Twilight Falls (Classic)"}}
E["npc:aku-mai"] = {t="npc",n="Aku'mai",z="blackfathom",s="At Blackfathom Deeps, Aku'mai haunts the sunken ruins of Elune's temple along the Zoram Strand. An Old God's corruption tainted the temple's sacred Moon Well, and Aku'mai rose from the waters as its servant. The Twilight's Hammer now sacrifices innocents to Aku'mai for power.",h="At Blackfathom Deeps, Aku'mai haunts the sunken ruins of Elune's temple along the Zoram Strand.",sec={{t="The Scourge of Zoram Strand",b="Blackfathom Deeps was once a great temple of Elune, until an Old God's corruption tainted its sacred Moon Well. Aku'mai, a gargantuan hydra and servant of the Old God, rose from the waters. Now Aku'mai lairs in the submerged ruins of the night elves' fallen temple, a blight upon the Zoram Strand whose malice poisons the waters.",sp=0},{t="Servant of the Primordial Darkness",b="Aku'mai's presence drew the Twilight's Hammer into the subterranean caverns. Led by Twilight Lord Kelris and allied with the naga, the cultists occupy the drowned temple and sacrifice innocents to Aku'mai for power.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is an ancient, three-headed hydra that serves an Old God. Aku'mai rose from Blackfathom Deeps' tainted waters and lairs in the temple's submerged halls.",al={"who is akumai","akumai lore","what kind of monster is akumai"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Aku'mai live?",a="Aku'mai lives in the submerged grottos of Blackfathom Deeps, a ruined temple of Elune along the Zoram Strand in north-western Ashenvale.",al={"akumai location","where is akumai","where can i find akumai"},it="place"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer feeding Aku'mai?",a="The Twilight's Hammer reveres Aku'mai as a servant of the Old Gods. Led by Twilight Lord Kelris, the cultists sacrifice innocents to Aku'mai for dark power.",al={"why are cultists feeding akumai","kelris akumai","twilights hammer akumai"},it="motive"},{q="What powers does Aku'mai possess?",a="Aku'mai is immense, with multiple snapping heads, and carries the dark favor of the Old Gods. In battle, Aku'mai rages and engulfs those nearby in clouds of poison.",al={"akumai powers","is akumai magical","void hydra"},it="power"},{q="Is Aku'mai an Old God?",a="No. Aku'mai is a primordial hydra that serves an Old God. Its evil presence drew the Twilight's Hammer to worship around it.",al={"is akumai an old god","is akumai a god"},it="origin"},{q="Why do adventurers venture into the deeps to slay it?",a="If left unchecked, Aku'mai's savagery and the cult's devotion threaten to unleash calamitous evil across Ashenvale and Kalimdor. Alliance and Horde authorities seek to end the Twilight's Hammer and slay the horror in the heart of the temple.",al={"why kill akumai","blackfathom villainy akumai","akumai threat"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Aku'mai on?",a="Aku'mai serves an Old God and holds no allegiance to mortal races. The Twilight's Hammer cult worships the beast and sacrifices innocents to it in exchange for dark power.",al={"akumai faction","who does akumai serve","akumai loyalty"},it="side",add="055a774d"},{q="What does Aku'mai want?",a="Aku'mai is a savage beast, not a schemer. A servant of an Old God, it lurks in the tainted waters of Blackfathom Deeps, and the Twilight's Hammer cultists who sacrifice innocents to it hope to bring back the era when the Old Gods ruled the world.",al={"akumai goal","what does akumai desire","akumai purpose"},it="wants",add="7b9e18bb"},{q="Why is Aku'mai here in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Aku'mai rose from the waters of the sunken temple when the corruption of an Old God seeped up from beneath the earth and tainted its sacred Moon Well. The drowned halls of Blackfathom Deeps now give the Twilight's Hammer cult a dark, watery haven where it can shelter and worship the beast in secret.",al={"why is akumai in blackfathom","how did akumai get here","akumai zhang strand"},it="why_here",add="6cae52d5"},{q="Who is Aku'mai tied to?",a="Aku'mai is a servant of an Old God. In Blackfathom Deeps, the Twilight's Hammer under Twilight Lord Kelris worships the beast and sacrifices innocents to it for power.",al={"akumai connections","who controls akumai","akumai and kelris"},it="ties",add="ba41fb22"},{q="Why is Aku'mai so feared?",a="Aku'mai is a gargantuan, three-headed hydra and servant of an Old God, risen from the tainted waters of the Zoram Strand. Tales of its savagery and the dark worship it draws from the Twilight's Hammer make it one of the most dreaded evils lurking along the Ashenvale coast.",al={"why is akumai feared","akumai reputation","is akumai dangerous"},it="fame",add="989c4b42"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Aku'mai has defiled the deepest sanctorum of a ruined temple once consecrated to Elune, turning a holy site into a lair of corruption.",["class:Priest"]="Aku'mai and the Twilight's Hammer embody the Old Gods' corruption, set against the teachings of the Holy Light and Elune.",["class:Druid"]="Aku'mai's unnatural corruption warps Ashenvale's coastal waters, which must be cleansed to restore natural balance."},kw={"aku'mai","akumai","blackfathom","deeps","hydra","kelris","old god","zoram"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","subzone:zoram-strand","quest:1200","topic:elune"},src={"Aku'mai"}}
E["npc:argent-guard-manados"] = {t="npc",n="Argent Guard Manados",z="blackfathom",s="At the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, Argent Guard Manados watches for corruption across Kalimdor. He serves the Argent Dawn and sends adventurers toward Blackfathom Deeps.",h="At the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, Argent Guard Manados watches for corruption across Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Sentinel of the Dawn",b="Argent Guard Manados keeps the Argent Dawn's watch in Darnassus. While most of the order guards Lordaeron against the Scourge, he stands among the artisans and tradefolk of the Craftsmen's Terrace. His post lets him watch for threats to northern Kalimdor's balance. When word reaches him that the Twilight's Hammer has gained a foothold beneath Ashenvale's waves, he calls on capable heroes to strike at Blackfathom Deeps and recover the cult's artifacts of dark devotion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Argent Guard Manados?",a="Manados is a night elf of the Argent Dawn, stationed in Darnassus. He watches Kalimdor for dark cults and otherworldly corruption while the order focuses on the Scourge in the Eastern Kingdoms.",al={"who is manados","argent guard manados role","manados darnassus"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Argent Guard Manados?",a="You can find Manados in Darnassus, standing in the Craftsmen's Terrace. He watches over the city and coordinates with local adventurers.",al={"manados location","where is argent guard manados","manados craftsman terrace"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Argent Guard Manados give?",a="Manados offers Twilight Falls. He sends adventurers into Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale to retrieve Twilight Pendants from the cultists within.",al={"manados quests","twilight falls quest giver","blackfathom deeps argent dawn quest"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn interested in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Argent Dawn watches for malignant forces threatening Azeroth. The Twilight's Hammer cult has emerged in Ashenvale's submerged ruins, worshipping ancient, corrupt entities, and the order cannot ignore that peril.",al={"why argent dawn bfd","argent dawn twilight cult"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Argent Guard Manados on?",a="Argent Guard Manados serves the Argent Dawn, an independent order dedicated to eradicating evil and protecting Azeroth from dark corruption. Though he is a night elf stationed within the capital city of Darnassus, his primary allegiance lies with the Dawn's global crusade rather than standard Alliance command.",al={"manados faction","who does manados serve","is manados alliance"},it="side",add="df5dd966"},{q="What does Argent Guard Manados want?",a="Manados seeks to stop the dark rituals taking root along the Ashenvale coast. He enlists capable adventurers to delve into Blackfathom Deeps and strike against the Twilight's Hammer cultists who have desecrated the ancient night elven sanctuary.",al={"what is manados looking for","manados goals","why send to blackfathom"},it="wants",add="f4cc0234"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Manados shows that duty can reach beyond the Cenarion Circle and the Sentinels. Some night elves serve neutral orders such as the Argent Dawn to preserve Azeroth.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion visiting Darnassus, you can turn to Manados for a link between the distant crusades in Lordaeron and the growing cultist threat in northern Kalimdor."},kw={"argent dawn","argent guard manados","blackfathom deeps","craftsmen's terrace","darnassus","manados","twilight falls"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","zone:darnassus","zone:blackfathom","quest:1199","subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace","topic:night-elf"},src={"Argent Guard Manados"}}
E["npc:baron-aquanis"] = {t="npc",n="Baron Aquanis",z="blackfathom",s="Blackfathom Deeps is where the Twilight's Hammer has made its lair, and Baron Aquanis rises from its flooded Moonshrine Ruins. He appears when someone disturbs the Fathom Stone, while the Earthen Ring suspects the cult has corrupted him.",h="Blackfathom Deeps is where the Twilight's Hammer has made its lair, and Baron Aquanis rises from its flooded...",sec={{t="Guardian of the Fathom Stone",b="The Fathom Stone lies beneath the flooded halls of the Moonshrine Ruins, right under the noses of the Twilight's Hammer cultists who occupy them. Within the stone rests a fathom core, a device that reveals the history of nearby elemental activity when properly read. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring sends Horde adventurers to recover it. Disturbing the stone draws Baron Aquanis up from the depths.",sp=0},{t="Corruption of the Depths",b="The Earthen Ring has long considered Baron Aquanis a corrupted elemental power. When he is destroyed, he leaves behind a Strange Water Globe, an impervious orb filled with putrid, sloshing water that seems to have fed him energy. Je'neu Sancrea believes the globe may prove what corrupted the baron and how. He would not be surprised if the Twilight's Hammer were responsible.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Baron Aquanis?",a="Baron Aquanis dwells in the flooded Moonshrine Ruins deep inside Blackfathom Deeps. He rises from the water when someone disturbs the underwater Fathom Stone, as Horde adventurers do while recovering its fathom core for Je'neu Sancrea.",al={"aquanis location","where is baron aquanis","how to spawn baron aquanis"}},{q="What is the Strange Water Globe?",a="The Strange Water Globe is what Baron Aquanis leaves behind when he is destroyed. The impervious orb holds putrid, sloshing water that seems to have fed his elemental energy. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring wants to study it for proof of what corrupted the baron and how.",al={"strange water globe","aquanis globe","what is the water globe for"}},{q="Why is the Earthen Ring interested in Baron Aquanis?",a="The Earthen Ring watches over the balance of the elements. Je'neu Sancrea and his comrades have long considered Baron Aquanis a corrupted elemental power. With the Twilight's Hammer in the Moonshrine Ruins, they fear the cult may be coercing the elements to work against the Horde. The baron's remains and the fathom core could show what the cult is doing.",al={"why earthen ring care","je'neu sancrea aquanis"}},{q="What is the Fathom Core?",a="The fathom core is an elemental artifact housed within the sunken Fathom Stone. Properly read by a trained shaman, it reveals a comprehensive history of regional elemental activity and can expose whatever dark rituals the Twilight's Hammer is conducting in the ruins.",al={"fathom core lore","what does fathom core do"}},{q="Is Baron Aquanis allied with the Twilight's Hammer?",a="As far as anyone can tell, Baron Aquanis is a corrupted elemental rather than a willing servant. The Twilight's Hammer cultists occupying the Moonshrine Ruins are the obvious suspects. Je'neu Sancrea says their involvement would not surprise him, but he wants proof before saying for sure.",al={"is aquanis twilight hammer","aquanis cult"}},{q="Does the Alliance have business with Baron Aquanis?",a="Not directly. The Fathom Stone and Baron Aquanis are Je'neu Sancrea's concern. He is an Earthen Ring shaman working with the Horde on Ashenvale's coast, and he sends Horde adventurers to recover the fathom core. Alliance explorers in Blackfathom Deeps have other errands there.",al={"can alliance fight aquanis","alliance aquanis quest"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="For shamans of the Earthen Ring, Baron Aquanis is a tragic example of elemental perversion. His tainted remains offer insight into purifying twisted spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="Je'neu Sancrea works with the Horde on Ashenvale's coast. The fathom core his Horde helpers recover is meant to show what the Twilight's Hammer is doing to the elements there."},kw={"aquanis","baron aquanis","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","fathom core","fathom stone","je'neu sancrea","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer","water elemental"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","npc:je-neu-sancrea","quest:6921","quest:6922","item:fathom-core","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:horde"},src={"Baron Aquanis","Baron Aquanis (quest)","Amongst the Ruins"}}
E["npc:dawnwatcher-selgorm"] = {t="npc",n="Dawnwatcher Selgorm",z="blackfathom",s="At the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, Dawnwatcher Selgorm watches for threats across northern Kalimdor. The human serves the Argent Dawn as an observer and liaison in the night elven capital, tracking reports of shadowy cult activity and dark powers stirring nearby.",h="At the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, Dawnwatcher Selgorm watches for threats across northern Kalimdor.",sec={{t="Eyes in the World Tree",b="Dawnwatcher Selgorm keeps watch in Darnassus for the Argent Dawn. The order's fight against the undead Scourge in the Eastern Plaguelands does not end its vigilance elsewhere. From the Craftsmen's Terrace, Selgorm gathers reports of emerging threats in Kalimdor's wilds. He connects the night elves with the wider effort against ancient evil and seeks Alliance travelers able to strike at cultists and dark powers before their influence spreads.",sp=0},{t="A Strike Against Darkness",b="Blackfathom Deeps, beneath the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale, draws Selgorm's attention. The Twilight's Hammer cult and serpentine naga have gathered in the flooded ruins. Selgorm rewards seasoned champions who venture there, targeting the cult's leaders and reclaiming tainted relics in hopes of quelling the shadows threatening Kalimdor's sacred shores.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Selgorm?",a="Dawnwatcher Selgorm is a human agent of the Argent Dawn, stationed in Darnassus to watch for encroaching evil across Kalimdor.",al={"selgorm","who is selgorm","dawnwatcher selgorm lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Dawnwatcher Selgorm be found?",a="Dawnwatcher Selgorm can be found outdoors on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, overlooking the night elven capital's workshops.",al={"selgorm location","where is selgorm","selgorm darnassus"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is an Argent Dawn member stationed in Darnassus?",a="The Argent Dawn fights the Scourge in Lordaeron and seeks to root out malevolence everywhere. In Darnassus, Selgorm watches for rising cult activity, including the Twilight's Hammer in northern Kalimdor.",al={"argent dawn in darnassus","why is argent dawn here"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Selgorm ask adventurers to do?",a="Selgorm awaits Alliance heroes returning from Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale with the head of Twilight Lord Kelris, the Twilight's Hammer leader there. The wounded Argent Guard Thaelrid urges them to slay Kelris and stop the cult's corruption from spreading.",al={"selgorm quest","blackfathom villainy quest giver"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Dawnwatcher Selgorm on?",a="Selgorm is an agent of the Argent Dawn, a neutral order dedicated to safeguarding Azeroth from corruption and darkness. While the Dawn operates independently of factional politics, Selgorm makes his camp among the night elves in Darnassus to solicit help from Alliance champions willing to strike at vile cults.",al={"selgorm faction","who does selgorm serve","is selgorm alliance"},it="side",add="7dd87e6e"},{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Selgorm tied to?",a="Selgorm answers directly to the Argent Dawn. Though stationed in the night elf capital of Darnassus, his duty is tied to his order's global vigil rather than the Kaldorei leadership, monitoring shadowy threats that fester far from the order's primary strongholds in the Plaguelands.",al={"selgorm argent dawn","who does selgorm work with","selgorm allies"},it="ties",add="6f2227e4"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer exploring northern Kalimdor, you can look to Selgorm as a link between Darnassus and the fight against sinister cults along the coast.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveling among Teldrassil's remote boughs, you may find a fellow countryman serving the Argent Dawn."},kw={"argent dawn","blackfathom deeps","blackfathom villainy","craftsmen's terrace","darnassus","dawnwatcher selgorm","twilight's hammer"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","zone:darnassus","subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace","quest:1200","zone:blackfathom","topic:alliance","quest:940"},src={"Dawnwatcher Selgorm"}}
E["npc:dawnwatcher-shaedlass"] = {t="npc",n="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass",z="blackfathom",s="In Darnassus, Dawnwatcher Shaedlass keeps watch for the Argent Dawn across Kalimdor. From the Craftsmen's Terrace, he seeks word of his fellow order members sent to scout hostile lands.",h="In Darnassus, Dawnwatcher Shaedlass keeps watch for the Argent Dawn across Kalimdor.",sec={{t="Eyes of the Argent Dawn",b="The Argent Dawn fights the Scourge in the Eastern Plaguelands, yet its watch reaches beyond Lordaeron. Dawnwatcher Shaedlass keeps the order's interests in Kalimdor from the night elf capital of Darnassus. At his post on the Craftsmen's Terrace, he follows covert expeditions against dark cults and corrupting powers that threaten the wider world.",sp=0},{t="A Missing Brother",b="Argent Guard Thaelrid is missing after a journey south to investigate cult activity in Blackfathom Deeps, along the Ashenvale coast. Shaedlass fears the Twilight's Hammer and the ancient elven temple's aquatic horrors may have harmed his comrade. He calls on daring Alliance adventurers to enter the ruins and learn what became of the scout.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Shaedlass?",a="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass is a night elf agent of the Argent Dawn, posted on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus. He connects the order with its efforts in northern Kalimdor.",al={"who is shaedlass","dawnwatcher shaedlass lore","argent dawn darnassus npc"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an Argent Dawn member in Darnassus?",a="The Argent Dawn fights the Scourge in Lordaeron, and keeps watch across Azeroth for corrupting evils. In Kalimdor, Shaedlass tracks threats such as shadowy cults.",al={"why is argent dawn in darnassus","argent dawn night elf"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Shaedlass ask adventurers to do?",a="Shaedlass sends Alliance adventurers into the sunken temple of Blackfathom Deeps to find Argent Guard Thaelrid. Thaelrid went undercover to investigate the Twilight's Hammer and has not reported back.",al={"shaedlass quest","in search of thaelrid quest"},it="wants"},{q="Where can I find Dawnwatcher Shaedlass?",a="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass is on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, near the capital's trade vendors and craftsmen.",al={"shaedlass location","where is dawnwatcher shaedlass"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Dawnwatcher Shaedlass on?",a="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass serves the Argent Dawn, a neutral coalition dedicated to fighting evil wherever it threatens Azeroth. Though he is a night elf residing in the capital city of Darnassus, his primary allegiance lies with the Dawn rather than strictly the Alliance, allowing him to focus on broader perils like cultists and the Scourge.",al={"shaedlass faction","who does shaedlass serve","is shaedlass alliance"},it="side",add="87de680c"},{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Shaedlass tied to?",a="Shaedlass answers directly to the Argent Dawn. He is particularly concerned with the fate of his fellow agent, Argent Guard Thaelrid, who was sent to investigate the foul corruption taking root within Blackfathom Deeps along the coast of Ashenvale.",al={"shaedlass connections","who does shaedlass work with","shaedlass argent dawn ties"},it="ties",add="e7a15b6d"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance heroes in Darnassus, Shaedlass offers a path into the mysteries of Blackfathom Deeps and sends scouts to recover an operative deep behind enemy lines.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf serving openly with the Argent Dawn, Shaedlass links Teldrassil's insular politics with the order's watch against darkness across the world."},kw={"argent dawn","blackfathom deeps","craftsmen's terrace","darnassus","dawnwatcher","shaedlass","thaelrid"},rel={"quest:1198","zone:darnassus","subzone:craftsmen-s-terrace","topic:argent-dawn","zone:blackfathom","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Dawnwatcher Shaedlass"}}
E["npc:gelihast"] = {t="npc",n="Gelihast",z="blackfathom",s="In Blackfathom Deeps, Gelihast guards a strange altar in the flooded Pool of Ask'ar. His Blindlight murlocs gather around him in the sunken temple.",h="In Blackfathom Deeps, Gelihast guards a strange altar in the flooded Pool of Ask'ar.",sec={{t="A Deadly Calling",b="Deep beneath the Zoram Strand, Gelihast has claimed a lair in Blackfathom Deeps. Most murlocs keep to coastal shallows, but he strikes at intruders with twin swords, moving too quickly for many to react. Casters who come within his reach rarely survive.",sp=0},{t="Master of the Blindlight",b="Gelihast rules the Pool of Ask'ar with his Blindlight brood, who swarm to his side at the first sign of trouble. An altar stands beyond his lair. Those who defeat him and touch it receive the Blessing of Blackfathom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gelihast?",a="Gelihast commands the Blindlight tribe in the Pool of Ask'ar, deep within Blackfathom Deeps. He fights with twin blades at blinding speed.",al={"who is gelihast","gelihast lore","gelihast background"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Gelihast inside Blackfathom Deeps?",a="No one knows what first drew Gelihast to Blackfathom Deeps. He and his Blindlight murlocs have claimed the Pool of Ask'ar in the flooded ruins, which he defends savagely against intruders.",al={"why is there a murloc in bfd","why is gelihast in the temple"},it="why_here"},{q="How did the Twilight's Hammer react to him?",a="Nothing is recorded of Gelihast's dealings with the Twilight's Hammer cultists deeper in the temple. He rules his own pool with his Blindlight murlocs.",al={"gelihast and twilights hammer","do cultists like gelihast"},it="side"},{q="What is the altar behind Gelihast?",a="An altar stands beyond Gelihast's pool. Travelers who defeat him can touch it to receive the Blessing of Blackfathom.",al={"altar of the deep","gelihast altar","blessing of blackfathom altar"}},{q="What tribe of murlocs does he lead?",a="Gelihast leads the Blindlight murlocs, an aggressive tribe that infests the Pool of Ask'ar within the caverns.",al={"gelihast tribe","what murlocs are in bfd"},it="ties"},{q="What happens to Gelihast if he is left unchecked?",a="Gelihast and his Blindlight murlocs keep the Pool of Ask'ar closed to anyone seeking to venture deeper into the sunken temple.",al={"gelihast fate","who kills gelihast"}},{q="What does Gelihast want?",a="Gelihast wants to keep his hold on the Pool of Ask'ar. With his Blindlight murlocs swarming around him, he savagely cuts down anyone who intrudes on his waters in the sunken temple.",al={"gelihast goal","what does gelihast want","gelihast motive"},it="wants",add="18aa1a09"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Gelihast attacks with blinding sword speed. As a warrior, you can brace yourself and turn his frantic dual-blade assault against him.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer seeking to cleanse the corruption leaking into Ashenvale, you must remove Gelihast to secure the submerged temple's northern passages.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde adventurer sent to scour Blackfathom Deeps, you must eliminate Gelihast to clear the way deeper into the sunken temple beneath the Zoram Strand."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","blindlight","gelihast","murloc","pool of ask'ar","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:murloc","npc:lady-sarevess"},src={"Gelihast"}}
E["npc:gershala-nightwhisper"] = {t="npc",n="Gershala Nightwhisper",z="blackfathom",s="In Auberdine, Gershala Nightwhisper studies what magical corruption does to elves. Concerned by the path taken by the high elves of Quel'Thalas, he examines cursed aquatic and demonic creatures for signs of how corruption changes mind and body.",h="In Auberdine, Gershala Nightwhisper studies what magical corruption does to elves.",sec={{t="Study of Transformation",b="From Auberdine, Gershala Nightwhisper looks beyond Darkshore's coastal troubles to the danger he sees in the high elves of Quel'Thalas. He watches with dismay as they embrace perilous arcane practices and call themselves blood elves. Gershala wants to understand the bodily and spiritual changes that follow unchecked magic. To study them, he sends seasoned Alliance adventurers into the submerged halls of Blackfathom Deeps to gather corrupted brain stems from the naga and satyr who dwell there.",sp=0},{t="An Antidote to Ruin",b="Gershala's interest in naga and satyr brain stems comes from their shared past. Both races were once night elves, before they yielded to Queen Azshara and demonic bargains. Gershala examines the marks that millennia of demonic and abyssal energies have left on their nervous systems. He hopes to find warnings or safeguards that might keep other elven kin from suffering similar monstrous deformity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Gershala Nightwhisper found?",a="Gershala Nightwhisper is found in Auberdine, the main Alliance port town on the coast of Darkshore.",al={"gershala location","where is gershala","find gershala nightwhisper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gershala want naga and satyr brain stems?",a="Gershala studies corrupted brain stems to examine how magical and demonic transformation changes the anatomy of former night elves. Both naga and satyr were once elves, and he seeks to understand the physical changes behind their corruption.",al={"why brain stems","researching the corruption lore","what does gershala study"},it="wants"},{q="What does Gershala hope to accomplish with his research?",a="Gershala hopes his research will help prevent the blood elves from becoming evil and monstrously deformed through their dangerous reliance on fel and unchecked arcane power.",al={"gershala goal","why help blood elves","gershala research purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where are the specimens Gershala needs located?",a="Gershala directs adventurers to Blackfathom Deeps, an ancient submerged temple ruin on the coast of Ashenvale, where naga and satyr dwell.",al={"where are the stems","blackfathom deeps stems","where to find gershala items"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is Gershala Nightwhisper?",a="Gershala Nightwhisper is a night elf scholar residing in the coastal settlement of Auberdine in Darkshore. Driven by scholarly curiosity and concern for the wider world, he dedicates himself to understanding magical and biological corruption. He studies the altered anatomy of creatures warped by dark powers, hoping that careful study can prevent similar downfalls among other peoples.",al={"who is gershala","gershala nightwhisper lore","gershala background"},it="identity",add="19945428"},{q="Whose side is Gershala Nightwhisper on?",a="Gershala is allied with the night elves of Darnassus and serves as a friendly scholar to members of the Alliance. His research takes place in Auberdine, where he works to protect Kalimdor and the broader mortal races from the creeping threats of demonic and magical degradation.",al={"gershala faction","is gershala alliance","gershala allegiance"},it="side",add="087b63f5"},{q="Why is Gershala Nightwhisper here?",a="Gershala makes his home in Auberdine because Darkshore lies directly adjacent to places deeply infested by ancient evils, such as Blackfathom Deeps. From this coastal haven, he can recruit travelers and adventurers venturing south to gather corrupted specimens for his ongoing research.",al={"why is gershala in auberdine","gershala purpose darkshore"},it="why_here",add="aee12c2d"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Gershala's grim inquiries recall the ancient Sundering and the terrible cost of magical addiction, which reshaped their brethren into horrors.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Gershala is a patron who sends expeditions into the hazards of Blackfathom Deeps, where they can gather valuable arcane knowledge."},kw={"auberdine","blackfathom","corruption","darkshore","gershala","naga","nightwhisper","satyr"},rel={"subzone:auberdine","zone:darkshore","quest:1275","zone:blackfathom","topic:night-elf","topic:satyr","topic:naga","quest:3765"},src={"Gershala Nightwhisper"}}
E["npc:ghamoo-ra-classic"] = {t="npc",n="Ghamoo-ra",z="blackfathom",s="In Blackfathom Deeps, Ghamoo-ra guards a small island in the Pool of Ask'ar. The ancient giant turtle tramples anyone who comes near.",h="In Blackfathom Deeps, Ghamoo-ra guards a small island in the Pool of Ask'ar.",sec={{t="A Beast of the Drowned Temple",b="Blackfathom Deeps was once a night elven temple to Elune. Flooded now, the ruins are claimed by naga, satyr, and the nihilistic Twilight's Hammer cult. Ghamoo-ra dwells among them, his enormous, thick shell turning aside all but the most determined blows.",sp=0},{t="Guardian of the Deeps",b="Lesser turtles surround Ghamoo-ra on a small island in the Pool of Ask'ar, and they leave travelers be. He alone attacks, crushing anyone who comes near beneath his trampling bulk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ghamoo-ra?",a="Ghamoo-ra guards a small island in the Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps, the flooded temple of Elune held by the Twilight's Hammer. He attacks anyone who approaches.",al={"ghamoo-ra lore","giant turtle bfd","who is ghamoo ra"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Ghamoo-ra hostile to outsiders?",a="Nothing is recorded of how Ghamoo-ra came to be so savage. He attacks anyone who intrudes on his island in the Pool of Ask'ar, trampling all who come near.",al={"why is turtle angry","why does turtle attack","ghamoo-ra madness"},it="hostile"},{q="Can a hunter tame Ghamoo-ra?",a="Yes. Despite his size and years of torment, a skilled hunter can tame Ghamoo-ra.",al={"tame ghamoo-ra","can hunter tame bfd turtle"},gp=true},{q="What is the Pool of Ask'ar?",a="The Pool of Ask'ar is a flooded subterranean cavern in Blackfathom Deeps. Ghamoo-ra roams the center of a small island there, surrounded by docile native turtles.",al={"pool of ask'ar","where is ghamoo ra"},it="place"},{q="What connection does he have to the Old Gods?",a="None is recorded. Ghamoo-ra is a beast of the deep, while Twilight's Hammer cultists who worship the Old Gods have overrun the sunken temple around him.",al={"ghamoo-ra old gods","is turtle corrupted"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Ghamoo-ra on?",a="Ghamoo-ra serves no one. He is a savage beast of the deep that attacks anyone who approaches his island in the Pool of Ask'ar, within the flooded temple the Twilight's Hammer now occupies.",al={"ghamoora faction","who does ghamoo-ra serve","is ghamoo-ra twilight hammer"},it="side",add="650cf597"},{q="What does Ghamoo-ra want?",a="Ghamoo-ra has no grand ambitions of his own. The giant turtle simply lashes out to crush intruders who come near his island in the Pool of Ask'ar.",al={"ghamoora goal","what does the turtle want","ghamoora motive"},it="wants",add="ff96574e"},{q="Why is Ghamoo-ra here?",a="Ghamoo-ra dwells on a small island in the Pool of Ask'ar, deep in Blackfathom Deeps, the flooded temple of Elune now overrun by naga, satyr and the Twilight's Hammer. How he came there is unrecorded.",al={"why is ghamoo-ra in blackfathom deeps","ghamoo-ra pool of ask'ar why","why is there a giant turtle here"},it="why_here",add="f3d3c23f"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter venturing into Blackfathom Deeps, you may pity Ghamoo-ra, a noble, ancient beast of the deep. With patience, you may yet tame him.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may see Ghamoo-ra's savage presence in Elune's drowned temple as a bitter reminder of how far the sacred site has fallen to the vile Twilight's Hammer.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you find in Ghamoo-ra an ancient creature of the deep, grown savage amid the ruins of the defiled temple."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","elune","ghamoo-ra","pool of ask'ar","tame","turtle","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:elune","topic:old-god"},src={"Ghamoo-ra (Classic)"}}
E["npc:je-neu-sancrea"] = {t="npc",n="Je'neu Sancrea",z="blackfathom",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Je'neu Sancrea watches the Ashenvale coast for dark disturbances. The Darkspear troll and Earthen Ring shaman sends Horde adventurers to investigate corruption in the submerged temple of Blackfathom Deeps.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Je'neu Sancrea watches the Ashenvale coast for dark disturbances.",sec={{t="A Shaman on the Strand",b="Je'neu Sancrea watches the dangerous Zoram Strand from Zoram'gar Outpost. While most of the Earthen Ring works to keep the elements in harmony across Kalimdor, he keeps watch over the coast. Dark tremors and unnatural tides stir near the ruined temple of Blackfathom Deeps. His shamanic duties bind him to the Earthen Ring, but his loyalties to the Darkspear tribe and Thrall's Horde lead him to work only with Horde champions.",sp=0},{t="Shadows of the Deep",b="Je'neu Sancrea seeks the cause of the corruption spreading along the coast. He gathers tainted sapphire cores and investigates the vile remains of water elementals, including Baron Aquanis. His inquiries reveal the influence of the Twilight's Hammer cult. Its rituals beneath the waves threaten the balance of the local elements and herald the return of forces sworn to the Old Gods.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll shaman of the Earthen Ring. He watches the corruption spreading from Blackfathom Deeps from his station at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Ashenvale coast.",al={"who is jeneu","jeneu sancrea lore","what is jeneu"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Je'neu only deal with Horde adventurers if he is Earthen Ring?",a="Je'neu's ties to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde guide whom he works with. The Earthen Ring seeks elemental balance, but Je'neu is stationed at a Horde outpost on the front line in Ashenvale and does not welcome Alliance travelers.",al={"why horde only","can alliance talk to jeneu","is jeneu neutral"},it="side"},{q="What is Je'neu investigating in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Je'neu investigates elemental unrest and dark magic rising from Blackfathom Deeps. He sends champions to recover corrupted water cores, slay Twilight's Hammer cultists, and confirm whispers that Aku'mai, an ancient hydra, serves malevolent masters beneath the sea.",al={"jeneu quest goals","what does jeneu want","why send players to bfd"},it="wants"},{q="Where is Je'neu Sancrea located?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is at Zoram'gar Outpost, a fortified Horde settlement on Ashenvale's far northwestern coast. The outpost lies along the Zoram Strand, just south of Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"where is jeneu","jeneu sancrea location","find jeneu"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Earthen Ring?",a="The Earthen Ring is an ancient circle of shamans devoted to understanding and calming the world's elemental spirits. Its members intervene when dark forces or chaotic entities upset the elements' natural harmony.",al={"earthen ring lore","what is the earthen ring","shaman organization"},it="ties"},{q="What is the threat of the Twilight's Hammer in the Deeps?",a="The Twilight's Hammer has infiltrated Blackfathom Deeps to worship Aku'mai and perform rituals for the Old Gods. Je'neu sends Horde adventurers against the cult's leaders to stop their work.",al={"twilights hammer bfd","twilight cult ashenvale","who are the cultists in bfd"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Je'neu Sancrea here?",a="Je'neu has stationed himself at the Zoram'gar Outpost along the Ashenvale coast to observe the sinister corruption stirring in the nearby ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. The Earthen Ring sensed foul disturbances in the natural balance of the waters, drawing him to this frontier to monitor the gathering cultists and enlist seasoned Horde champions to scour the depths.",al={"why is jeneu in ashenvale","why is jeneu sancrea at zoramgar","what brings jeneu sancrea here"},it="why_here",add="1670a3c0"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you follow the Earthen Ring's work to balance corrupted elementals and restore balance to Kalimdor's waters.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Je'neu for guidance as you enter Blackfathom Deeps from Ashenvale.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you share the Darkspear path into the Earthen Ring, alongside tauren and orc allies."},kw={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","je'neu sancrea","jeneu","twilight's hammer","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","npc:aku-mai","topic:twilight-s-hammer","quest:6564","quest:6563","quest:6922","quest:824"},src={"Je'neu Sancrea"}}
E["npc:lady-sarevess"] = {t="npc",n="Lady Sarevess",z="blackfathom",s="Within Blackfathom Deeps, Lady Sarevess works dark sorceries in the flooded ruins.",h="Within Blackfathom Deeps, Lady Sarevess works dark sorceries in the flooded ruins.",sec={{t="A Grotto in the Deeps",b="Lady Sarevess performs rituals in a flooded grotto within the Pool of Ask'ar. The Twilight's Hammer cultists haunt the sunken temple too, pursuing their own worship deeper in the cavern.",sp=0},{t="Sorcery of the Tides",b="Lady Sarevess commands elemental currents and crackling lightning. Loyal naga sentinels and summoned water elementals guard her sanctuary as she fights intruders who threaten her dark work.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lady Sarevess?",a="Lady Sarevess dwells in the subterranean Pool of Ask'ar inside Blackfathom Deeps. The very twisted naga spellcaster dabbles in dark magic.",al={"who is sarevess","sarevess lore","lady sarevess backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Lady Sarevess be found?",a="Lady Sarevess makes her lair in the Pool of Ask'ar, a flooded chamber in the early reaches of the Blackfathom Deeps temple complex along the Ashenvale coast.",al={"sarevess location","where is lady sarevess","pool of askar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What powers does Lady Sarevess command?",a="Lady Sarevess wields water and elemental magic, including violent bursts of forked lightning, against anyone who enters her cove.",al={"sarevess magic","sarevess abilities"},it="power"},{q="Whose side is Lady Sarevess on?",a="Lady Sarevess serves her own naga kin rather than the Alliance or the Horde. A very twisted spellcaster, she lairs in the flooded Pool of Ask'ar within Blackfathom Deeps and fiercely defends her grotto against any intruder.",al={"lady sarevess faction","who does sarevess serve","sarevess allegiance"},it="side",add="75d3f337"},{q="What does Lady Sarevess want?",a="Sarevess seeks to expand her mastery over twisted magical arts, conducting dark rituals in her flooded grotto deep within Blackfathom Deeps and striking down any intruder who disturbs her work.",al={"what is sarevess doing","lady sarevess goal","sarevess purpose"},it="wants",add="67d48548"},{q="Why is Lady Sarevess here in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Lady Sarevess has claimed the Pool of Ask'ar, a flooded grotto in the ruined temple of Blackfathom Deeps, as her lair. There she dabbles in dark magic, guarded by naga sentinels and summoned water elementals.",al={"why is lady sarevess in bfd","sarevess blackfathom deeps why","why is sarevess here"},it="why_here",add="6008d570"},{q="Who is Lady Sarevess tied to?",a="Sarevess is tied to the naga who infest the flooded ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, commanding loyal naga sentinels and summoned water elementals in her grotto. The Twilight's Hammer cultists who also haunt the sunken temple pursue their own worship deeper in the cavern.",al={"sarevess allies","who does sarevess work with","sarevess twilight hammer"},it="ties",add="d8505f38"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, the ruins Lady Sarevess inhabits were once a sacred temple of Elune. Her twisted naga kin defiling the waters of Ask'ar recalls the Sundering.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see how highborne magical practices became raw, chaotic lightning and tidal sorcery after centuries of oceanic corruption."},kw={"aku'mai","blackfathom deeps","lady sarevess","naga","pool of ask'ar","sarevess","sea witch","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga","topic:old-god"},src={"Lady Sarevess"}}
E["npc:lorgus-jett"] = {t="npc",n="Lorgus Jett",z="blackfathom",s="In Blackfathom Deeps, Lorgus Jett commands the Twilight's Hammer among flooded ruins. The Horde has marked him as a target.",h="In Blackfathom Deeps, Lorgus Jett commands the Twilight's Hammer among flooded ruins.",sec={{t="A Defiler in the Ruins",b="Lorgus Jett is a human among the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. While many cultists there are orcs or tauren, Jett ranges from the upper Moonshrine Ruins to the tunnels beyond Gelihast, the murloc defiler. He coordinates the cult's rituals and violent ambitions in the ancient night elf ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lorgus Jett?",a="Lorgus Jett serves the Twilight's Hammer inside Blackfathom Deeps. He oversees the cult's work in the Moonshrine Ruins and serves the Old Gods.",al={"lorgus jett lore","who is lorgus","lorgus jett background"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Lorgus Jett be found in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Lorgus Jett patrols the Moonshrine Ruins. He may be near the first groups of Twilight cultists or farther along the flooded passages past Gelihast's shrine.",al={"lorgus jett location","where is lorgus jett","find lorgus jett"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde want Lorgus Jett dead?",a="The Horde seeks Lorgus Jett's death through Allegiance to the Old Gods. His presence in Ashenvale threatens regional stability, and he serves an alliance devoted to unleashing ancient, world-ending entities.",al={"why kill lorgus","allegiance to the old gods quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does a human use shamanistic powers?",a="The Twilight's Hammer communes with chaotic elemental forces and the Old Gods rather than traditional ancestral spirits. That path lets humans wield elemental devastation.",al={"lorgus jett magic","human shaman lorgus"},it="power"},{q="What is Lorgus Jett's connection to Gelihast?",a="Lorgus Jett and Gelihast both dwell in the Moonshrine Ruins of Blackfathom Deeps and serve dark powers beneath the sea. Jett often patrols the corridors beyond Gelihast's altar.",al={"lorgus and gelihast","gelihast connection"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Lorgus Jett on?",a="Lorgus Jett serves the Twilight's Hammer, the apocalyptic cult dedicated to the Old Gods. Though a human, he has abandoned his kin to align himself with the dark ritualists and elemental forces congregating within the forgotten depths of Ashenvale.",al={"lorgus jett faction","who does lorgus jett serve","what faction is lorgus jett"},it="side",add="647bfdae"},{q="Why is Lorgus Jett in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="He lurks within the subterranean Moonshrine Ruins alongside his fellow cultists, carrying out the will of the Twilight's Hammer. Deep within the ancient elven temple, the cult tends to dark horrors and venerates the ancient powers stirring beneath the waters.",al={"why is lorgus jett in bfd","lorgus jett purpose blackfathom","why is lorgus jett here"},it="why_here",add="ba0235c4"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you wield the elements in harmony or reverence; Jett uses the Twilight's Hammer's corrupted, violent methods.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can help sever the Twilight's Hammer leadership beneath the Ashenvale shore by striking down Lorgus Jett.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you may find Jett's service to cosmic terrors far to the west in Kalimdor a chilling sign of the Twilight's Hammer's reach."},kw={"allegiance to the old gods","blackfathom deeps","lorgus jett","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","quest:6564","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","npc:gelihast","topic:old-god"},src={"Lorgus Jett"}}
E["npc:old-serra-kis"] = {t="npc",n="Old Serra'kis",z="blackfathom",s="Beneath the Moonshrine Sanctum, Old Serra'kis lurks in the flooded depths of Blackfathom Deeps. The enormous threshadon is hidden in a submerged cave, and deadly to anyone who seeks him there.",h="Beneath the Moonshrine Sanctum, Old Serra'kis lurks in the flooded depths of Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Unconquered in the Depths",b="The Twilight's Hammer has made its home in the sunken Moonshrine Ruins. Beneath the Moonshrine Sanctum, dark waters conceal older, wilder things. Old Serra'kis, the largest threshadon in the sunken temple, lurks in the Forgotten Pool, a flooded cave beneath the ruins where few would think to look.",sp=0},{t="A Hidden Threat",b="To reach Old Serra'kis, you must dive deep beneath the temple floor into a flooded cavern. No air pockets break the water, making the cave as deadly as the beast within. Cornered in the murk, Serra'kis shows an unnatural resilience. He drains life from his attackers with shadow energy, sustaining his own vitality in the darkness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is Old Serra'kis?",a="Old Serra'kis is a massive, ancient threshadon, a long-necked aquatic reptile native to Azeroth's lakes and coastal waters.",al={"what is serrakis","is serrakis a hydra","serrakis creature type"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't the Twilight's Hammer kill him?",a="Nothing records the cult hunting him. Old Serra'kis hides in the Forgotten Pool, a flooded, airless cave beneath the ruins, and is deadly to anyone who dives in after him.",al={"why is serrakis still alive","twilights hammer serrakis"},it="why_here"},{q="Where is Old Serra'kis located?",a="Old Serra'kis lurks in a submerged cavern beneath the water around the Moonshrine Sanctum in Blackfathom Deeps. You must dive under the ruins into an airless pool to encounter him.",al={"how to find serrakis","serrakis location","where is old serrakis"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What makes fighting him dangerous?",a="The fight takes place underwater, with no natural air pockets. Old Serra'kis leeches shadow energy from nearby foes to heal his wounds throughout the battle.",al={"serrakis abilities","how to beat serrakis"},it="danger"},{q="Does Serra'kis serve the Twilight's Hammer?",a="No. Unlike other beasts corrupted or trained by the cult, Old Serra'kis remains an untamed wild predator defending his subterranean lair.",al={"is serrakis a cultist pet","who controls serrakis"},it="side"},{q="Can you breathe during the battle with Serra'kis?",a="The enclosed cave has no air pockets near the ceiling. Underwater fighters must manage their breath, use magical water-breathing aid, or draw the beast toward open water.",al={"drowning serrakis","breath underwater serrakis"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Why is Old Serra'kis feared?",a="Old Serra'kis is the largest threshadon in Blackfathom Deeps, hidden in a flooded cave beneath the Moonshrine Ruins with no air to breathe. He drains the life from those who fight him to heal his own wounds, making him a deadly foe for anyone who dives in after him.",al={"serrakis reputation","why is serrakis famous","why fear serrakis"},it="fame",add="fc1a5d36"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid of the wild, Aquatic Form helps you dive into the lightless pool to confront this prehistoric predator.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can bestow Unending Breath, making an airless subterranean ambush manageable.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can use Water Breathing spells granted through communion with the elements to help your companions avoid drowning as they grapple with the ancient threshadon."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","forgotten pool","moonshrine sanctum","old serrakis","serrakis","threshadon","twilight's hammer","underwater boss"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-sanctum","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","subzone:forgotten-pool","topic:twilight-s-hammer","npc:ghamoo-ra-classic"},src={"Old Serra'kis"}}
E["npc:scout-thaelrid"] = {t="npc",n="Argent Guard Thaelrid",z="blackfathom",s="Wounded near the Pool of Ask'ar, Argent Guard Thaelrid is cut off in Blackfathom Deeps. The night elf scout entered the submerged ruins for the Argent Dawn, and now he has seen what gathers below.",h="Wounded near the Pool of Ask'ar, Argent Guard Thaelrid is cut off in Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Eyes of the Argent Dawn",b="Reports of foul rites beneath the sea reached the Argent Dawn from the Zoram Strand. The order watches for rising evils and unnatural corruption across Azeroth, so it sent Scout Thaelrid into Blackfathom Deeps. He was to judge the threat, watch the flooded temple, and report back. Then the Dawn could decide where aid was most needed.",sp=0},{t="A Grasping Darkness",b="Thaelrid found a threat far worse than the rumors suggested. Savage naga and the Twilight's Hammer cult have made an unholy pact in the submerged ruins. Under Twilight Lord Kelris, cultists offer blood sacrifices to feed the hydra Aku'mai and bargain with ancient terrors for dark power. Before Thaelrid could carry the warning to the surface, Blackfathom Deeps' denizens grievously wounded him. Cut off near the Pool of Ask'ar, he remains trapped.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Argent Guard Thaelrid?",a="Argent Guard Thaelrid is a night elf operative of the Argent Dawn. He entered Blackfathom Deeps along Ashenvale's coast to gather intelligence on the forces below.",al={"who is thaelrid","thaelrid lore","thaelrid background"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Thaelrid trapped inside Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps' denizens discovered and grievously wounded Thaelrid as he reconnoitered the temple. Unable to fight back to the surface alone, he took shelter near the Pool of Ask'ar.",al={"why is he stuck","how did he get wounded","why is thaelrid dying"},it="why_here"},{q="What did Thaelrid discover in the depths?",a="Thaelrid found an unholy pact between the naga and the Twilight's Hammer cult in Blackfathom Deeps. The cultists sacrifice blood to feed Aku'mai and bargain with ancient terrors for dark power.",al={"what did thaelrid find","what are the cultists doing","blackfathom secrets"}},{q="Who does Thaelrid work for?",a="Thaelrid serves the Argent Dawn, a neutral order that fights corruption, evil, and apocalyptic threats across Azeroth, whatever the faction lines.",al={"thaelrid faction","is thaelrid argent dawn","is thaelrid alliance"},it="side"},{q="What does Thaelrid ask adventurers to do?",a="Unable to leave his refuge, Thaelrid asks for Twilight Lord Kelris to be slain and the cult leader's head brought back as proof the threat is broken.",al={"thaelrid quest","blackfathom villainy quest","what does he want"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Thaelrid be found?",a="Thaelrid lies injured in a secluded alcove near the Pool of Ask'ar, just beyond Blackfathom Deeps' flooded preliminary caverns.",al={"where is thaelrid","thaelrid location","pool of askar scout"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Argent Guard Thaelrid tied to?",a="Argent Guard Thaelrid answers directly to the Argent Dawn. Charged with keeping watch against encroaching evils across Azeroth, the order dispatched him into the submerged temple of Blackfathom Deeps to verify alarming reports regarding the Twilight's Hammer cult and their newfound naga allies.",al={"thaelrid ties","who does thaelrid answer to","scout thaelrid argent dawn"},it="ties",add="879268fe"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, naga and doomsday cults defiling ancient temple grounds like Blackfathom is a bitter outrage. Thaelrid represents their people's vigil over Kalimdor's deepest wounds.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts follow up on Thaelrid's disappearance in Ashenvale, seeking to keep the Zoram Strand safe and support the Argent Dawn's neutral work.",["faction:Horde"]="Thaelrid is a night elf, but he serves the Argent Dawn. Any adventurer willing to strike at the Twilight's Hammer and cleanse the cavern can aid him."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","pool of ask'ar","scout thaelrid","thaelrid","twilight lord kelris"},rel={"quest:1198","quest:1200","zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","npc:aku-mai","topic:argent-dawn","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Scout Thaelrid"}}
E["npc:tsunaman"] = {t="npc",n="Tsunaman",z="blackfathom",s="At Sun Rock Retreat, Tsunaman watches the currents of Kalimdor for signs of unrest. He works with the Horde against forces that threaten the waters.",h="At Sun Rock Retreat, Tsunaman watches the currents of Kalimdor for signs of unrest.",sec={{t="Agent of the Tides",b="Near the path from Sun Rock Retreat down to the Charred Vale, Tsunaman serves the Tribunal of the Tides, high-ranking servants aligned with the Tidehunter, Neptulon. He works with the Horde to watch for elemental unrest throughout Kalimdor, especially disturbances spreading from the submerged caverns of Blackfathom Deeps.",sp=0},{t="Hatred of Flame",b="Tsunaman hates fire in every form. The burning lands of the Charred Vale and incursions by fire elementals keep him fuming. Around camp, he sometimes marches to nearby cooking fires and campfires and smacks them out with a heavy fist of water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tsunaman?",a="Tsunaman is a water elemental at Sun Rock Retreat in the Stonetalon Mountains. He serves the Tribunal of the Tides, watching elemental conflicts in Kalimdor and seeking aid against unnatural disturbances.",al={"who is tsunaman","tsunaman lore","what is tsunaman"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Tsunaman attack the campfire?",a="Tsunaman despises fire elementals and fire itself. At Sun Rock Retreat, he sometimes stomps over to travelers' campfires and extinguishes them with a watery strike.",al={"tsunaman punching fire","why does tsunaman hit fire","water elemental campfire"}},{q="What is the Tribunal of the Tides?",a="The Tribunal of the Tides is an order of powerful elemental lieutenants aligned with Neptulon the Tidehunter, the Elemental Lord of water. They oversee aquatic domains and respond to disruptions in the world's waters.",al={"tribunal of the tides","who does tsunaman serve"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Tsunaman interested in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps has been polluted by twilight cultists and dark forces that corrupt its native water spirits. Tsunaman enlists Horde adventurers to enter the sunken temple and quell the chaos in the waters.",al={"tsunaman blackfathom","trouble in the deeps"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Tsunaman on?",a="Tsunaman does not answer to the mortal races of the Horde or the Alliance. He serves the elemental powers of water, specifically the Tribunal of the Tides who stand as high-ranking lieutenants of Neptulon the Tidehunter. While he tolerates visitors at Sun Rock Retreat and enlists adventurers against common foes, his true loyalty lies entirely with the watery depths and his elemental brethren.",al={"tsunaman faction","who does tsunaman serve","tsunaman allegiance"},it="side",add="83418127"},{q="What does Tsunaman want?",a="Tsunaman is driven by the ancient elemental struggle. He seeks the eradication of rival fire elementals and despises flame in all its forms, regularly lashing out at even simple campfires. Furthermore, he works to advance the interests of the Tribunal of the Tides by recruiting capable mortals to address dark disturbances within aquatic sanctuaries like the Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"tsunaman goals","what is tsunaman trying to do","tsunaman desires"},it="wants",add="d98f482b"},{q="Why is Tsunaman here in Sun Rock Retreat?",a="Tsunaman stations himself along the trail leading out from Sun Rock Retreat toward the scorched lands of the Charred Vale. Positioned here on behalf of the Tribunal of the Tides, he watches the nearby elemental conflicts unfolding across the Stonetalon Mountains and reaches out to passing adventurers who can strike out against encroaching fiery adversaries or venture into troubled subterranean waters.",al={"why is tsunaman in stonetalon","tsunaman sun rock retreat reason","why did tsunaman come here"},it="why_here",add="37c31a70"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman seeking to understand and commune with the elements, you can speak directly with an emissary of the Tidehunter's court through Tsunaman.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can work with Tsunaman at Sun Rock Retreat against elemental imbalance and cultist intrusion in Kalimdor's waters."},kw={"charred vale","neptulon","stonetalon","sun rock retreat","tribunal of the tides","trouble in the deeps","tsunaman","water elemental"},rel={"quest:6562","subzone:sun-rock-retreat","zone:stonetalon","zone:blackfathom","subzone:charred-vale"},src={"Tsunaman"}}
E["npc:twilight-lord-kelris"] = {t="npc",n="Twilight Lord Kelris",z="blackfathom",s="At Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight Lord Kelris leads the Twilight's Hammer from the sunken ruins. The orc warlock holds high rank in the cult and directs its rites in the Moonshrine Sanctum. There, his followers worship Aku'mai and seek a reign of cosmic chaos.",h="At Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight Lord Kelris leads the Twilight's Hammer from the sunken ruins.",sec={{t="Herald of the Void",b="Twilight Lord Kelris directs the cultists who seized the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. For years, he slipped past watchful eyes in Darnassus and evaded the Argent Dawn. Whenever ancient malice stirred across Kalimdor, Kelris was suspected of being behind it. He pledged himself to the Old Gods, not to warlords or clans. He seeks to unmake mortal civilization and return Azeroth to primordial chaos.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of the Beast",b="In the Moonshrine Sanctum, Kelris oversees the cult's worship of Aku'mai, a vicious three-headed hydra who serves an Old God. Allied with the naga, the Twilight's Hammer occupies the drowned temple. Kelris leads the cult's rites and sacrifices innocents to Aku'mai in exchange for power.",sp=0},{t="Dark Trance and Slumber",b="Twilight Lord Kelris commands potent shadow magic that can seize minds and plunge intruders into deep, unnatural sleep. He prays without cease before a corrupted altar ringed by candles that channel dark energies. Anyone who tries to strike him down must defeat the cult leader and face the latent horrors stirred when his ritual vigil is broken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris is an orc sorcerer and high-ranking leader who commands the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. He directs the cult's activity throughout the sunken temple and is devoted to the Old Gods.",al={"kelris lore","who is kelris","kelris background"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn hunting Kelris?",a="The Argent Dawn hunts Kelris as an elusive instigator of malice throughout Kalimdor. Though he was once believed dead or missing, his hand was found behind numerous dark plots across the continent, making his elimination a priority.",al={"argent dawn kelris","why kill kelris","blackfathom villainy reason"},it="fame"},{q="What is Kelris doing with the hydra Aku'mai?",a="Kelris and his Twilight's Hammer cultists worship Aku'mai, a three-headed hydra who serves an Old God. The beast lairs in the deepest part of the sunken temple.",al={"kelris and akumai","why is kelris feeding akumai"},it="wants"},{q="What happens after Kelris is defeated?",a="Behind Kelris stands an altar with four ceremonial candles. Lighting them unbinds the sanctum's protective wards, summons waves of Aku'mai's servants, and opens the sealed gate to the beast's lair.",al={"kelris candles","altar of kelris","moonshrine candles"},sp=1},{q="What powers does Kelris use in combat?",a="Kelris uses potent shadow spells, mental domination, and magical slumber to incapacitate his enemies while his dark rites continue.",al={"kelris abilities","kelris spells"},it="power"},{q="Who is Bashana Runetotem?",a="Bashana Runetotem is Kelris's ally and investigates the corruption in Blackfathom Deeps. Bashana warns adventurers of Kelris's obsession with Old God worship and his desire to plunge the world back into primeval chaos.",al={"bashana runetotem kelris","tauren hunter kelris"}},{q="Whose side is Twilight Lord Kelris on?",a="Kelris leads the local cell of the Twilight's Hammer cult. He serves neither the Horde nor the Alliance, dedicating his life entirely to the worship and service of the ancient Old Gods and the return of primordial chaos to Azeroth.",al={"kelris faction","who does kelris serve","twilight lord kelris allegiance"},it="side",add="e447f79b"},{q="Why is Twilight Lord Kelris here in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Kelris leads the Twilight's Hammer in the sunken ruins, where the cult communes with the Old Gods and worships the hydra Aku'mai, a servant of an Old God. From the Moonshrine Sanctum he presides over their rites, far away from watchful eyes.",al={"why is kelris in bfd","kelris blackfathom purpose","why did kelris come here"},it="why_here",add="710418bf"},{q="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris tied to?",a="Beyond commanding the Twilight's Hammer cultists lurking in the cavern, Kelris presides over the cult's worship of the dread hydra Aku'mai. He also maintains ties to the Old Gods he worships, carrying out their dark designs across Kalimdor.",al={"kelris allies","who does kelris work with","kelris connections"},it="ties",add="7c0659ed"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="The Argent Dawn, operating from Darnassus, seeks to end Kelris's elusive career of stirring dark cults and terror across northern Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Elders and shamans see Kelris as a cautionary abomination, an orc who abandoned the elements and ancestral spirits to grovel before ancient cosmic horrors.",["class:Warlock"]="Typical warlocks bargain with demons of the Burning Legion. Kelris shows the shadow magic born from yielding to Old God whispers, which can induce a trance.",["race:NightElf"]="Kelris's blasphemous rites despoil the Moonshrine Sanctum, an ancient elven temple dedicated to Elune."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","blackfathom deeps","kelris","moonshrine sanctum","old gods","twilight lord","twilight's hammer"},rel={"quest:1200","npc:aku-mai","subzone:moonshrine-sanctum","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","topic:argent-dawn","npc:bashana-runetotem"},src={"Twilight Lord Kelris"}}
E["quest:1198"] = {t="quest",n="In Search of Thaelrid",z="blackfathom",s="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass sends you into Blackfathom Deeps to find the scout who went missing there. The Argent Dawn fears naga and Twilight's Hammer cultists have joined forces in the flooded ruins.",h="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass sends you into Blackfathom Deeps to find the scout who went missing there.",sec={{t="Eyes in Darnassus",b="The Argent Dawn watches for threats across Kalimdor as well as the Scourge in Lordaeron. Dawnwatcher Shaedlass gathers reports from Darnassus about unnatural dangers. Word reaches him that naga and the doomsday zealots of the Twilight's Hammer have made a pact in Blackfathom Deeps, the flooded ruins along the Ashenvale shore. The order fears what this alliance could bring.",sp=0},{t="The Missing Scout",b="Argent Guard Thaelrid entered the caverns to investigate the coastal rumors. Weeks have passed without word, and Shaedlass's other scouts are away on separate operations. He fears Thaelrid has fallen or been captured by the dark powers beneath the waves. Now he asks you to enter Blackfathom Deeps and bring the missing scout back alive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Argent Dawn interested in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Argent Dawn watches for threats across Azeroth, including dangers beyond the undead of the Eastern Kingdoms. Naga joining forces with Twilight's Hammer cultists in Kalimdor demands the order's attention.",al={"why argent dawn here","argent dawn blackfathom","argent dawn naga"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Shaedlass?",a="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass is an Argent Dawn operative in Darnassus, the night elf capital. He gathers information, finds where the order's aid is needed, and sends investigators to assess regional crises.",al={"who is shaedlass","quest giver shaedlass","dawnwatcher shaedlass role"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Argent Guard Thaelrid?",a="Argent Guard Thaelrid is an Argent Dawn operative sent to investigate Blackfathom Deeps. He was sent to learn the strength and intent of the naga and cultists in the drowned caverns.",al={"who is thaelrid","thaelrid lore","missing scout thaelrid"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Thaelrid be found?",a="Argent Guard Thaelrid is deep inside Blackfathom Deeps, along the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale. He has infiltrated the caverns and waits there alone for reinforcements.",al={"thaelrid location","where is thaelrid","find thaelrid bfd"},gp=true},{q="What happens after finding Thaelrid?",a="When Thaelrid is found, he reveals the true nature of the ritual in the ruins and points you toward the cult's leaders in Blackfathom Villainy.",al={"what comes next","followup to thaelrid","next quest after thaelrid"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can Horde players take this mission?",a="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass gives the assignment in Darnassus, and it is aimed at Alliance adventurers. Horde adventurers can accept it if they reach him.",al={"horde in search of thaelrid","can horde do this quest","horde thaelrid"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dawnwatcher Shaedlass want you to find Thaelrid?",a="Shaedlass gathers intelligence for the Argent Dawn to monitor growing evils across Kalimdor. Weeks ago, he dispatched Argent Guard Thaelrid to investigate disturbing rumors regarding an alliance between the naga and the Twilight's Hammer in Blackfathom Deeps. With no word returned from him, he fears the worst and needs to confirm both the status of the scout and the truth behind the sinister plot taking root along the Ashenvale coast.",al={"why find thaelrid","shaedlass motive","why send to blackfathom deeps"},it="motive",add="4b9c6d96"},{q="Why does Shaedlass send an adventurer instead of his own scouts?",a="The Argent Dawn's presence in Darnassus is thin, and Shaedlass notes that all of his other scouts are fully preoccupied with their own urgent missions across the land. With Thaelrid missing and no available agents left to spare, he must rely on capable and willing adventurers to enter the treacherous depths on his behalf.",al={"why me in search of thaelrid","why not send argent dawn scouts"},it="why_me",add="3832a285"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, you can begin serving alongside the Argent Dawn and earn its goodwill.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the ancient Temple of Elune in Blackfathom Deeps has been defiled. Helping the Argent Dawn means recovering sacred night elven heritage.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin aligned with the Argent Dawn, you recognize Thaelrid's lonely vigil as a solemn duty to guard the world against shadow and corruption."},kw={"argent dawn","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","darnassus","naga","shaedlass","thaelrid","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:dawnwatcher-shaedlass","zone:blackfathom","quest:1200","topic:argent-dawn","zone:darnassus","zone:ashenvale","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga"},m={start="Dawnwatcher Shaedlass",["end"]="Argent Guard Thaelrid",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=1198},src={"In Search of Thaelrid"}}
E["quest:1199"] = {t="quest",n="Twilight Falls",z="blackfathom",s="At Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight's Hammer cultists join with naga beneath the Ashenvale coast. Argent Guard Manados in Darnassus calls on Alliance champions to gather pendants from the fallen cultists and hinder their plans to awaken ancient evils.",h="At Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight's Hammer cultists join with naga beneath the Ashenvale coast.",sec={{t="A Sanctum Defiled",b="Beneath Ashenvale's Zoram Strand, Blackfathom Deeps lies in ruins. The night elf temple was once sacred to Elune and held a powerful moonwell, until the Sundering shattered it and plunged it beneath the sea. Now naga and cultists fill its halls. The waters have turned foul, and the cultists revere powers darker than the sea.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of the Old Gods",b="Twilight's Hammer worships the chaotic Old Gods and seeks their return, hoping to spread madness and ruin across the world. Reports in Darnassus say the cultists have joined with the naga in Blackfathom Deeps. In the submerged halls, they perform rituals and use the temple's tainted waters to feed their dark masters' resurgence.",sp=0},{t="The Vigil of the Argent Dawn",b="Argent Guard Manados watches over threats to Azeroth from Darnassus on behalf of the Argent Dawn. He sees the danger in Blackfathom Deeps: its horrors could reach every civilized race. The order offers aid and recognition to heroes who enter the flooded labyrinth, cull the cultists, and bring back the Twilight Pendants from their necks as proof of their defeat.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Argent Guard Manados?",a="Argent Guard Manados is an Argent Dawn emissary stationed in Darnassus. He watches for cults and dark forces threatening Kalimdor and enlists adventurers to destroy them.",al={"manados","who gives twilight falls","argent guard manados location"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the Argent Dawn concerned about Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Argent Dawn fights the Scourge in Lordaeron, but its charter also covers unnatural evils that threaten the world. Old God worship and the alliance between cultists and naga in Kalimdor could bring catastrophe if left unchecked.",al={"why argent dawn darnassus","argent dawn blackfathom"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Twilight's Hammer?",a="Twilight's Hammer is a doomsday cult devoted to the chaotic Old Gods, primordial beings imprisoned beneath the earth long ago. Its followers seek an apocalyptic end that would let their masters rise and remake the world in terror and madness.",al={"twilight hammer cult","who are twilight's hammer","twilights hammer"},it="target"},{q="What were the Twilight Pendants used for?",a="Twilight Pendants are dark talismans worn by Twilight's Hammer members to show their allegiance to the entities they worship. The Argent Dawn gathers them as proof that a cultist has been slain and neutralized.",al={"twilight pendant lore","what are twilight pendants"},it="item"},{q="What was Blackfathom Deeps originally?",a="Blackfathom Deeps was a night elf temple dedicated to Elune, famed for its powerful moonwell. The Great Sundering broke the earth and submerged its halls beneath the sea.",al={"blackfathom history","bfd temple history","blackfathom moonwell"},it="place"},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer working with the naga?",a="The reasons for the union are not fully known. Both groups are drawn to the dark power stirring in the sunken temple. The cultists gain safe access to ancient submerged chambers, while the naga benefit from their sorceries and sacrificial rites.",al={"naga cultists alliance","bfd naga alliance"},it="allies"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, the desecration of a sacred temple and moonwell by Old God cultists and naga affronts Elune and Ashenvale's ancestral lands.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, Twilight's Hammer threatens from just south of Darkshore, and clearing Blackfathom Deeps helps secure northern Kalimdor.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin aligned with orders like the Argent Dawn, you see Twilight's Hammer's Old God worship as an abomination that demands righteous cleansing.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you sense the corruption of the temple's once-sacred moonwell and the maddening, shadowy whispers driving the cultists deeper into madness."},kw={"argent dawn","argent guard manados","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","darnassus","manados","naga","old gods","twilight falls","twilight pendant","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:argent-guard-manados","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:argent-dawn","topic:old-god","topic:naga","zone:darnassus","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Argent Guard Manados",level="25",faction="Alliance",id=1199,ri={"Twilight Pendant"}},src={"Twilight Falls (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1200"] = {t="quest",n="Blackfathom Villainy",z="blackfathom",s="At Blackfathom Deeps, Argent Guard Thaelrid calls for the Alliance to stop Twilight Lord Kelris. The cult leader sacrifices captives to Aku'mai, and Thaelrid asks for Kelris's severed head as proof to bring to the Argent Dawn in Darnassus.",h="At Blackfathom Deeps, Argent Guard Thaelrid calls for the Alliance to stop Twilight Lord Kelris.",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Blackfathom Deeps was once a night elven temple devoted to Elune. Corruption from an ancient Old God rose through the rock, fouling the Moon Well and freeing Aku'mai, a voracious servant of that darkness. The Twilight's Hammer joined with local naga after the temple was defiled, making its holy halls a place of ritual murder.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Guard's Plea",b="Argent Guard Thaelrid entered Blackfathom Deeps on behalf of his order, but was grievously wounded and drained of strength. Surrounded by enemies, he knows he cannot finish his mission alone. He pleads with brave Alliance travelers who reach him to kill Twilight Lord Kelris, the cultist leading sacrifices of innocents to Aku'mai in exchange for dark power.",sp=0},{t="Justice in Darnassus",b="At the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus, the severed head of Kelris is presented to Dawnwatcher Selgorm, bringing a long and troubling hunt to an end. The Argent Dawn feared Kelris was dead or lost to the shadows, for he had been involved time and again when dark forces stirred in Kalimdor. His death secures a vital victory against the cult's designs in Ashenvale.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Argent Guard Thaelrid?",a="Thaelrid is an Argent Dawn operative sent to investigate the growing shadow within Blackfathom Deeps. Grievously wounded in the depths, his strength is spent, so he recruits passing adventurers to stop Kelris.",al={"who is thaelrid","thaelrid lore","argent guard"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Twilight Lord Kelris being targeted?",a="Kelris leads the Twilight's Hammer cultists in Blackfathom Deeps. He sacrifices innocent captives to Aku'mai, a foul beast linked to the Old Gods, in exchange for malevolent power.",al={"who is kelris","why kill kelris","twilight lord kelris"},it="target"},{q="Who is Dawnwatcher Selgorm?",a="Dawnwatcher Selgorm is an Argent Dawn representative stationed on the Craftsmen's Terrace in Darnassus. He oversees the order's efforts against encroaching corruption across northern Kalimdor.",al={"selgorm darnassus","who is selgorm","argent dawn darnassus"},it="identity"},{q="What is the history of Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Before Blackfathom Deeps became a sunken lair, its caverns held a great night elven temple devoted to Elune. The temple fell into ruin after an Old God's malice rose up and fouled its sacred Moon Well.",al={"bfd history","what was blackfathom deeps","temple of elune bfd"},it="history"},{q="Who is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is a monstrous, hydra-like servant of an Old God that crawled from the tainted waters beneath Blackfathom Deeps. The Twilight's Hammer reveres Aku'mai and feeds it captives for dark blessings.",al={"what is akumai","aku'mai lore","akumai beast"},it="identity"},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer and naga working together?",a="The reason for the pact between the Twilight's Hammer and the naga is not fully known. In Blackfathom Deeps, they have joined forces to occupy the ruined temple grounds while the cult sacrifices captives to Aku'mai.",al={"naga cultists alliance","why are naga in bfd","twilight hammer and naga"},it="allies"},{q="Why does Argent Guard Thaelrid want Twilight Lord Kelris slain?",a="Thaelrid has uncovered that Twilight Lord Kelris and his cultists are sacrificing innocent captives to Aku'mai, a servant of an Old God, in exchange for dark power. As an agent of the Argent Dawn, Thaelrid is dedicated to halting such evil and ending the gruesome ritual slaughter taking place within the ruined temple.",al={"thaelrid motive","why does thaelrid want kelris dead","why kill kelris"},it="motive",add="96533b2d"},{q="What is the Head of Kelris for?",a="The head serves as undeniable proof of the cult leader's demise. Dawnwatcher Selgorm and the Argent Dawn believed Kelris was dead or missing after years of elusive villainy across Kalimdor. Bringing his head to Selgorm in Darnassus confirms that his reign of terror and blood sacrifices have finally come to an end.",al={"head of kelris","why do i need kelris's head","what to do with kelris head"},it="item",add="101c08a2"},{q="Why can't Argent Guard Thaelrid slay Kelris himself?",a="Thaelrid is deep within the flooded ruins, wounded and completely exhausted. His strength has left him, and he cannot fight his way through the cultists and naga, let alone strike down Kelris on his own. He relies on you to finish the mission in his stead.",al={"why doesn't thaelrid fight kelris","why does thaelrid need me","can thaelrid kill kelris"},it="why_me",add="5d00ba2b"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, avenging the defilement of an ancient temple of Elune and cleansing its poisoned Moon Well strikes at the heart of kaldorei heritage.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help the Argent Dawn protect Ashenvale's vulnerable borders from cult infiltration by aiding them against Kelris.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, answering the Argent Dawn's call to slay a cultist who sacrifices innocents to primordial horrors is holy retribution.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, stopping Kelris ends the blasphemous desecration of waters once held holy in devotion to the divine."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","blackfathom","darnassus","deeps","elune","kelris","moon well","selgorm","thaelrid","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:twilight-lord-kelris","quest:1198","npc:dawnwatcher-selgorm","zone:blackfathom","npc:aku-mai","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:argent-dawn","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Argent Guard Thaelrid",["end"]="Dawnwatcher Selgorm",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1200,ri={"Head of Kelris"}},src={"Blackfathom Villainy (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:1275"] = {t="quest",n="Researching the Corruption",z="blackfathom",s="In Auberdine, Gershala Nightwhisper seeks corrupted brain stems from Blackfathom Deeps. Reports say blood elves across the sea are turning to demonic magic, and he hopes to learn from the naga and satyr before history repeats itself.",h="In Auberdine, Gershala Nightwhisper seeks corrupted brain stems from Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Warning from History",b="The ruin of their ancient kin remains a living memory to night elves across Kalimdor. Ten thousand years ago, the Highborne gave in to demonic energies and became horned satyrs or serpentine naga. Now the high elves call themselves blood elves and embrace dark magic. Gershala Nightwhisper sees the old disaster taking shape again.",sp=0},{t="Into the Deeps",b="Blackfathom Deeps offers Gershala a place to study the corruption. The temple ruins lie beneath the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale, where satyr cultists and naga dwell. He asks you to gather brain stems from both, hoping to trace the link between arcane addiction, demonic corruption, and the ruin of the body.",sp=0},{t="A Desperate Cure",b="Gershala says he studies the body to find a way to prevent another fall. He believes the shared mutations of satyrs and naga may show how to draw the blood elves back from damnation. Can research in Darkshore sway the desperate elves of Quel'Thalas? That remains uncertain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Gershala Nightwhisper care about the blood elves?",a="Gershala fears the blood elves' turn to demonic powers could create another race of twisted monsters, as elven hubris once gave rise to satyrs and naga.",al={"why help blood elves","gershala blood elf connection","auberdine blood elves"},it="motive"},{q="Where do you gather the corrupted brain stems?",a="Gather the brain stems from satyrs and naga in Blackfathom Deeps, an ancient temple complex beneath the Zoram Strand on Ashenvale's northwest coast.",al={"where are brain stems","brain stem location","corrupt brain stem drop"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does he specifically want satyr and naga samples?",a="Satyrs and naga both began as elves warped by unnatural forces: satyrs through demonic bargains, and naga through the Sundering. Gershala compares their brain mutations to learn how dark power harms elven bodies.",al={"why satyr and naga","satyr naga connection"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who leads you to this task?",a="An introductory trail called The Corruption Abroad can lead you to Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine. He can also offer the investigation directly.",al={"prerequisite quest","corruption abroad connection"},it="origin"},{q="What does Gershala plan to do with the specimens?",a="Gershala plans to compare the bodily effects of the two corruptions, hoping what he learns can slow the blood elves' descent into monstrosity.",al={"brain stem study","gershala research goal"},it="item"},{q="Is Auberdine directly threatened by Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps lies just across Ashenvale's southern border. The night elves of Auberdine watch the coast for signs of worsening demonic and Twilight corruption.",al={"why auberdine cares","blackfathom deeps threat darkshore"},it="threat"},{q="Who are you sent against in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Gershala sends you against the satyrs and naga dwelling within Blackfathom Deeps along the coast of Ashenvale. Both species were once night elves before undergoing grotesque magical transformations—the satyrs warped by demonic corruption during the War of the Ancients, and the naga mutated by ancient dark powers beneath the sea. Now, both factions inhabit the submerged temple ruins.",al={"what enemies for researching corruption","who do i fight blackfathom deeps","researching the corruption targets"},it="target",add="57dc4e51"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you face a wound still alive in your people's memory: your kin became the satyrs and naga who plague Kalimdor.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you feel revulsion toward satyrs, whose fel corruption defiles the natural dream and warps the land.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you see the bodily and spiritual cost of reckless dependence on magic.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you hear reports of blood elves turning to dark arts across the sea and fear a new demonic threat."},kw={"ashenvale","auberdine","blackfathom deeps","blood elves","corrupted brain stem","corruption abroad","gershala nightwhisper","naga","satyr"},rel={"npc:gershala-nightwhisper","quest:3765","zone:blackfathom","subzone:auberdine","topic:satyr","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Gershala Nightwhisper",level="24",faction="Alliance",id=1275,ri={"Corrupted Brain Stem"}},src={"Researching the Corruption (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6561"] = {t="quest",n="Blackfathom Villainy",z="blackfathom",s="Inside Blackfathom Deeps, Blackfathom Villainy reaches a wounded scout who cannot finish his mission alone. Argent Dawn scout Thaelrid asks passing Horde champions to end Twilight Lord Kelris's blood sacrifices to Aku'mai in the sunken ruins.",h="Inside Blackfathom Deeps, Blackfathom Villainy reaches a wounded scout who cannot finish his mission alone.",sec={{t="A Desperate Last Stand",b="Argent Dawn scout Thaelrid lies wounded in the underground temple along the Ashenvale coast. His reconnaissance uncovered horrors beyond naga incursions, but his strength is spent and he cannot complete the mission alone. He calls on passing Horde champions to strike at the cult's leaders in the sunken halls.",sp=0},{t="Sacrifices to the Deep",b="Twilight Lord Kelris leads the Twilight's Hammer cultists within the ruined Temple of the Moon. With the local naga, he performs dark rites over the defiled Moon Well. Captives are fed alive to Aku'mai, a ravenous hydra and beast of the Old Gods, as Kelris seeks cosmic power and primordial chaos.",sp=0},{t="Word to Thunder Bluff",b="Argent Dawn believed Kelris dead or lost, so word of his fate matters. Thaelrid directs proof of the cult leader's death to Bashana Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Attuned to the Earthmother's natural balance, Bashana honors the victory over a corruption bent on dragging Kalimdor into primeval ruin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris leads the Twilight's Hammer cultists in Blackfathom Deeps. Argent Dawn believed him dead or missing, but he has gathered power by sacrificing captives to the ancient hydra Aku'mai in the corrupted Moon Well.",al={"kelris","who is kelris","twilight lord kelris"},it="target"},{q="Why is an Argent Dawn member inside Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Argent Dawn scout Thaelrid entered the ruined night elf temple to investigate its growing threat. The dangers there left him mortally weakened and trapped, so he relies on visiting adventurers to finish his duty and kill Kelris.",al={"argent guard thaelrid","why is thaelrid here","argent dawn in bfd"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is an ancient, monstrous hydra with many heads, regarded as a primordial servant of the Old Gods. It woke when corruption from deep underground tainted the temple's sacred waters, and now devours captives brought by the Twilight's Hammer.",al={"akumai","who is akumai","aku'mai lore"},it="danger"},{q="Why turn the quest in to Bashana Runetotem?",a="Thaelrid sends Horde champions to Bashana Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. As a steward of the Earthmother's balance, Bashana keeps in touch with defenders against ancient evil and sees Kelris's Old God worship as a blight upon Kalimdor.",al={"bashana runetotem","why thunder bluff","where to turn in blackfathom villainy"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps was once a subterranean temple sacred to the moon goddess Elune. Upheaval and ancient darkness seeping from the earth tainted the great Moon Well, and naga and doomsday cultists claimed the sunken sanctuaries for their dark master Aku'mai.",al={"history of blackfathom deeps","temple of elune ruins","why is bfd corrupted"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the goal of the Twilight's Hammer cult here?",a="The Twilight's Hammer seeks to return the world to primordial chaos through worship of the Old Gods. Kelris seeks power through dark communion, feeding innocents to the depths to win the favor of ancient beings.",al={"twilight's hammer motives","why cult in bfd","kelris goals"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Argent Guard Thaelrid want Twilight Lord Kelris slain?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris and his Twilight's Hammer cultists are actively sacrificing innocent captives to Aku'mai, a foul servant of the Old Gods, in exchange for dark power. Thaelrid was sent by the Argent Dawn to stop these horrors, and he cannot allow the cult's depravities and chaotic worship to continue unchecked.",al={"thaelrid motive","why does thaelrid want kelris dead","why kill kelris"},it="motive",add="8c6f2eb7"},{q="Why does Thaelrid need your help instead of stopping Kelris himself?",a="Thaelrid has been grievously wounded deep within the sunken temple. Weakened, drained, and completely out of strength, he cannot face the cult leader on his own, leaving you as the only one capable of finishing his mission.",al={"why does thaelrid need help","why can't thaelrid fight kelris","thaelrid why me"},it="why_me",add="f2efcdf9"},{q="What is the Head of Kelris for?",a="The head serves as undeniable proof of the cult leader's demise. Kelris had long evaded the Argent Dawn, leading many to believe he was already dead or lost, so presenting his head to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff confirms that his reign of terror and human sacrifice has truly ended.",al={"head of kelris purpose","what to do with head of kelris","why take kelris's head"},it="item",add="6dbae1c3"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, joining forces with an Argent Dawn scout is an uncommon act of shared purpose against a cosmic blight, and earns the Dawn's early favor.",["race:Tauren"]="Bashana Runetotem sees Kelris's defeat as a defense of the Earthmother, cleansing an abomination that sought to drive the world's natural order into primeval chaos.",["class:Druid"]="For a druid, the naga and void-worshipping cultists' defilement of an ancient night elf Moon Well wounds Kalimdor's natural and spiritual sanctuary.",["class:Shaman"]="For a shaman, Kelris and Aku'mai disturb elemental balance, turning pure underground waters into a place of shadow and sacrifice."},kw={"aku'mai","argent dawn","bashana runetotem","blackfathom deeps","blackfathom villainy","kelris","moon well","thaelrid","twilight lord kelris","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","npc:aku-mai","npc:bashana-runetotem","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:argent-dawn","topic:old-god","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Argent Guard Thaelrid",["end"]="Bashana Runetotem",level="27",faction="Horde",id=6561,ri={"Head of Kelris"}},src={"Blackfathom Villainy (Horde)"}}
E["quest:6562"] = {t="quest",n="Trouble in the Deeps",z="blackfathom",s="Tsunaman sends Horde travelers from Stonetalon Mountains to aid Je'neu Sancrea on Ashenvale's remote coast. The troll scholar waits at Zoram'gar Outpost, where danger gathers along the shore.",h="Tsunaman sends Horde travelers from Stonetalon Mountains to aid Je'neu Sancrea on Ashenvale's remote coast.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Coast",b="Tsunaman hears troubling reports from the north and calls on Horde travelers to reach Je'neu Sancrea. The troll scholar is at Zoram'gar Outpost, on Ashenvale's far western shore, the Zoram Strand. Je'neu faces mounting danger and needs help from beyond the outpost.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Zoram Strand",b="The road to Ashenvale's western shore is dangerous for Horde travelers. You can pass through Windshear Crag, disturbed by goblins, or travel north from the Barrens. Either way, you enter forest watched by night elf sentinels. Far beneath Ashenvale's dense canopy, Zoram'gar Outpost holds on along the storm-washed Zoram Strand, facing the shadowed waters.",sp=0},{t="Whispers Below the Waves",b="At the shore, Je'neu Sancrea points to trouble beneath the tides, in the sunken temple of Blackfathom Deeps. Ancient corruption, foul water elementals and Twilight's Hammer cultists gather there, stirring ancient evils. Je'neu looks to arriving champions to enter the submerged halls and face the terror rising within.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Trouble in the Deeps?",a="Tsunaman, in the Stonetalon Mountains, sends Horde travelers to aid allies along Ashenvale's coast.",al={"quest giver","who starts trouble in the deeps","tsunaman"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Je'neu Sancrea located?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand, along Ashenvale's far western coast.",al={"where is je'neu","jeneu sancrea location","zoram'gar outpost"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you reach Zoram'gar Outpost from Stonetalon?",a="From Stonetalon, travel northeast through Windshear Crag into Ashenvale, or east through the Barrens and enter the forest from the south. Then head west from central Ashenvale to the Zoram Strand.",al={"path to ashenvale","how to get to zoram strand","stonetalon to ashenvale route"},gp=true},{q="What trouble is Je'neu investigating?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is watching the ruins of Blackfathom Deeps, where cultists and corrupted aquatic beings stir ancient horrors beneath the surface.",al={"what is happening at zoram strand","why does jeneu need help"},it="threat"},{q="What quest follows Trouble in the Deeps?",a="Je'neu Sancrea sends you into Blackfathom Deeps to gather the elementally charged Sapphires of Aku'Mai from its tunnels.",al={"next quest","trouble in the deeps follow up"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is the journey through Ashenvale considered perilous?",a="Night elves fiercely defend Ashenvale from Horde incursions. Hostile sentinels and hidden ambushers threaten travelers in the forest.",al={"ashenvale danger","night elf threat"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Tsunaman send you to Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Tsunaman knows that Je'neu Sancrea is isolated at the remote Zoram'gar Outpost and in desperate need of capable allies. Stationed on the far western coast of Ashenvale, Je'neu faces mounting dangers surrounding the mysterious depths of Blackfathom Deeps without sufficient support. Tsunaman dispatches you to reinforce him before hostile forces overwhelm the Horde's foothold.",al={"why does tsunaman want this done","why send me to ashenvale","tsunaman motive"},it="motive",add="dde1b6c4"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you help hold Zoram'gar Outpost on Kalimdor's western flank against night elf forces and coastal horrors.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can read the disturbance in Zoram Strand's water spirits and help cleanse the corruption threatening them.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can aid Je'neu Sancrea, one of the Darkspears' foremost scholars, as he uncovers ancient mysteries of Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","je'neu sancrea","stonetalon mountains","tsunaman","windshear crag","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:tsunaman","npc:je-neu-sancrea","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:zoram-strand","zone:ashenvale","zone:stonetalon","zone:blackfathom","quest:6563"},m={start="Tsunaman",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",level="22",faction="Horde",id=6562},src={"Trouble in the Deeps"}}
E["quest:6563"] = {t="quest",n="The Essence of Aku'Mai",z="blackfathom",s="Je'neu Sancrea has found the naga harvesting sapphires in Blackfathom Deeps. At Zoram'gar Outpost, the shaman asks Horde adventurers to recover them before their power is misused.",h="Je'neu Sancrea has found the naga harvesting sapphires in Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Threat in the Depths",b="Je'neu Sancrea watches over the Kaldorei ruins from the Zoram Strand. Naga now mine sapphire clusters in the submerged chambers of Blackfathom Deeps, where the gems grow along damp cavern walls. Sancrea senses the serpentine invaders mean to harness their power and seeks to stop the harvest before they can use it.",sp=0},{t="Water Spirits and Arcane Power",b="The Sapphires of Aku'mai carry elemental water energy and hold clinging water spirits. Adept sorcerers could use them to fuel dangerous arcane rituals or strengthen Aku'mai, the shadowy hydra whose presence fills the subterranean temple. Recovering the clusters keeps this potent reagent from the naga and helps guard the coastline against unchecked elemental magic.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Je'neu Sancrea, a Darkspear troll shaman, gives the request at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand in north-western Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","who starts essence of akumai","jeneu sancrea location"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the naga want the Sapphires of Aku'Mai?",a="The naga's exact purpose is unknown, but the sapphires hold potent elemental water energy and raw magical power that could fuel their spells.",al={"why do naga want sapphires","what are the crystals for","sapphire purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where are the sapphire clusters found?",a="Sapphire clusters line the cavern walls and floors in Blackfathom Deeps' outer tunnels and flooded passages, just inside the ruined underground entrance along the Zoram Strand.",al={"where to find sapphires","sapphire of akumai location","crystal spawns"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Aku'mai?",a="Aku'mai is a monstrous three-headed hydra dwelling deep within the submerged temple ruins. Twilight's Hammer cultists revere him as a servant of the Old Gods.",al={"who is akumai","what is akumai","aku'mai"},it="threat"},{q="Do I have to kill any dungeon bosses for this quest?",a="No. The sapphire clusters grow in the earlier submerged tunnels, before you encounter Blackfathom Deeps' main bosses.",al={"do i need a full group","can i solo sapphires","boss requirement"},gp=true},{q="Does this quest connect to any other storyline?",a="Yes. It follows 'Trouble in the Deeps' and continues Je'neu Sancrea's investigation into the rising darkness and cultist activity in Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"quest chain","prerequisites","trouble in the deeps"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Je'neu Sancrea want the Sapphires of Aku'Mai?",a="Je'neu Sancrea noticed the naga systematically harvesting these crystal clusters from the cavern walls of Blackfathom Deeps. While their exact scheme remains unclear, he senses immense elemental energy lingering within the stones. He wants them collected before the naga can weaponize them as potent arcane components.",al={"jeneu sancrea motive","why gather sapphires","why collect sapphires of akumai"},it="motive",add="7dd39a86"},{q="What is the Sapphire of Aku'Mai?",a="These sapphires are crystalline formations lining the submerged tunnels of Blackfathom Deeps. They resonate with raw elemental power, drawing water spirits to cling to them. Because of this natural concentration of energy, they serve as formidable arcane reagents if properly channeled.",al={"what are the sapphires","sapphire of akumai lore","sapphires of akumai power"},it="item",add="644dacf9"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can sense the restless water spirits bound within the crystals, a warning of corrupted elemental forces beneath the temple.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help guard the perilous foothold at Zoram'gar Outpost by keeping nearby naga from gaining raw magical power.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can look to Je'neu Sancrea, an observant Darkspear mystic who relies on communion with the spirits and ancestral wisdom to face the strange threats of Kalimdor."},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","je'neu sancrea","naga","sapphire of aku'mai","trouble in the deeps","water spirits","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","quest:6562","zone:blackfathom","subzone:zoram-strand","npc:aku-mai","topic:naga","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Je'neu Sancrea",level="22",faction="Horde",id=6563,ri={"Sapphire of Aku'Mai"}},src={"The Essence of Aku'Mai (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6565"] = {t="quest",n="Allegiance to the Old Gods",z="blackfathom",s="At Zoram'gar, the Horde moves against the Twilight's Hammer cult in Blackfathom Deeps. Je'neu Sancrea sends champions after Lorgus Jett to disrupt the cultists who seek to awaken ancient forces of destruction beneath Ashenvale's coast.",h="At Zoram'gar, the Horde moves against the Twilight's Hammer cult in Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="The Threat Beneath Zoram'gar",b="Zoram'gar Outpost watches Blackfathom Deeps from the Ashenvale shore. Naga, corrupted beasts, and Twilight's Hammer fanatics overrun the submerged temple complex. Je'neu Sancrea, an Earthen Ring seer stationed on the coast, sees that the cultists serve the Old Gods rather than the land's natural balance and spirits. These monstrous beings of chaos were defeated in ancient times, yet their malign touch still lingers in Azeroth's forgotten places.",sp=0},{t="Ending Lorgus Jett",b="Je'neu sends Horde champions into the underground ruins to hunt Lorgus Jett, a key leader among the cultists established in Blackfathom Deeps. Lorgus works deep in the stone passages between the chambers of Ghamoo-ra, the giant turtle, and Baron Aquanis, the water elemental. Je'neu is too frail to enter the damp darkness himself. Lorgus's defeat is vital to severing the dark rituals he sought to orchestrate beneath Ashenvale's waves.",sp=0},{t="Staving off Chaos",b="Lorgus Jett's death contains the immediate ritual threat to the coast, though Je'neu knows the Twilight's Hammer remains active. Its quiet infiltration of ancient holy sites points to a wider menace seeking the return of the Old Gods. At Zoram'gar, Lorgus's defeat buys the Horde time against an enemy hidden in the world's shadows.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lorgus Jett?",a="Lorgus Jett is an established leader of the Twilight's Hammer cultists in Blackfathom Deeps. He directs rituals meant to bring back the ancient Old Gods and their rule.",al={"lorgus jett","who is lorgus","lorgus jett lore"},it="target"},{q="Where can Lorgus Jett be found in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Lorgus Jett patrols Blackfathom Deeps' flooded corridors, in the connecting halls between Ghamoo-ra's chamber and Baron Aquanis's altar area.",al={"lorgus jett location","where is lorgus","find lorgus jett"},gp=true},{q="Who is Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is a Darkspear troll seer of the Earthen Ring, stationed at Zoram'gar Outpost on the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale. He watches elemental disturbances and the corruption in Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"je'neu sancrea","who gives allegiance to the old gods","jeneu"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Je'neu care about the Twilight's Hammer?",a="Je'neu is dedicated to understanding nature and elemental balance, and sees the Twilight's Hammer as an existential threat. The cult serves the chaotic Old Gods, whose return would undo the world's harmony.",al={"why fight twilight hammer","earthen ring old gods"},it="motive"},{q="What are the Old Gods?",a="The Old Gods are primordial beings of chaos and destruction who ruled Azeroth in the distant past before they were defeated and buried. The Twilight's Hammer worships them and schemes to break their seals, bringing back their destructive rule.",al={"old gods lore","who are old gods","creatures of chaos"},it="threat"},{q="Why can't Je'neu Sancrea kill Lorgus Jett himself?",a="Je'neu is too frail to brave Blackfathom Deeps alone. He tracks spiritual and elemental disturbances from the outpost while Horde champions do the fighting.",al={"why jeneu doesnt go","is jeneu weak"},it="why_me"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Defeating Lorgus Jett protects Zoram'gar Outpost and its isolated Horde encampment from insidious cultist plots.",["class:Shaman"]="The Twilight's Hammer seeks to unleash elemental fury for the chaotic Old Gods. Eradicating the cult is a priority for those sworn to elemental balance alongside the Earthen Ring.",["race:Troll"]="Helping Je'neu Sancrea honors the wisdom of a respected Darkspear seer working far from the Echo Isles to protect Azeroth's primal spirits."},kw={"allegiance to the old gods","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","je'neu sancrea","lorgus jett","old gods","twilight's hammer","zoram'gar"},rel={"npc:lorgus-jett","npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","npc:ghamoo-ra-classic","quest:6922","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Je'neu Sancrea",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",level="26",faction="Horde",id=6565},src={"Allegiance to the Old Gods (2)"}}
E["quest:6921"] = {t="quest",n="Amongst the Ruins",z="blackfathom",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Je'neu Sancrea sends Horde adventurers into Blackfathom Deeps for a fathom core. The Earthen Ring hopes the relic will reveal what the Twilight's Hammer is doing with the elements.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Je'neu Sancrea sends Horde adventurers into Blackfathom Deeps for a fathom core.",sec={{t="A Threat in the Deep",b="The Twilight's Hammer has taken hold of Blackfathom Deeps, the ancient night elven temple once sacred to Elune. Its cultists command the submerged passages. At Zoram'gar Outpost on Ashenvale's shore, Darkspear shaman Je'neu Sancrea watches the corruption spread. He fears the cult means to bend the local elements against the land and its defenders.",sp=0},{t="The Fathom Stone",b="Je'neu Sancrea sends Horde champions to retrieve a fathom core from the fathom stone beneath the waters of the Moonshrine Ruins. Shamans who can decipher the core will find a detailed record of elemental currents and disturbances. The Earthen Ring hopes the relic will expose the Twilight's Hammer's work and help keep the region safe from elemental disaster.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Amongst the Ruins?",a="Je'neu Sancrea gives the task. The Darkspear troll serves the Earthen Ring at Zoram'gar Outpost, along the Zoram Strand in western Ashenvale.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest","who starts amongst the ruins"},it="identity"},{q="What is a fathom core?",a="A fathom core is an artifact held within a submerged fathom stone in the ruins. Shamans can read it for a record of elemental activity, including how the local elements are being forced and manipulated.",al={"what is the fathom core","fathom stone purpose","what does the core do"},it="item"},{q="Why is the Earthen Ring concerned about Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Earthen Ring seeks balance among the elements. The Twilight's Hammer has taken over the submerged ruins and is corrupting and coercing the elements, threatening the region's stability.",al={"earthen ring motive","why does the earthen ring care","blackfathom deeps cultists"},it="threat"},{q="Where is the fathom stone located?",a="The fathom stone lies beneath the waters of the Moonshrine Ruins inside Blackfathom Deeps. Explorers must dive below the surface to retrieve its core.",al={"where is the stone","fathom core location","moonshrine ruins fathom core"},gp=true},{q="Can Alliance players take this quest?",a="No. Only Horde adventurers can take on this work. Je'neu Sancrea is based at the Horde outpost of Zoram'gar and supports the Horde's presence in Ashenvale while serving the Earthen Ring.",al={"is this horde only","alliance version","can alliance do amongst the ruins"},it="side",gp=true},{q="What group is occupying Blackfathom Deeps?",a="The Twilight's Hammer occupies Blackfathom Deeps. The cult serves sinister Old God beings and twists the elements toward catastrophic ends.",al={"who is in blackfathom","enemies in bfd","twilight's hammer blackfathom"},it="hostile"},{q="Why does Je'neu Sancrea want the Fathom Core recovered?",a="Je'neu Sancrea fears that the Twilight's Hammer cultists occupying Blackfathom Deeps will coerce the local elements into turning against the region and the Horde. Without the Fathom Core, the Earthen Ring is blind to what rituals and elemental disturbances the cult is conducting deep beneath the ruins.",al={"jeneu sancrea motive","why get the fathom core","why amongst the ruins"},it="motive",add="139b4a2b"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, retrieving the fathom core helps the Earthen Ring protect the spirits of water and earth from the Twilight's Hammer's coercion.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, clearing threats from Blackfathom Deeps helps protect Zoram'gar Outpost and the Horde's foothold on Ashenvale's coast.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, aiding Je'neu Sancrea means helping a fellow Darkspear who connects the Horde with the Earthen Ring's elemental caretakers."},kw={"amongst the ruins","ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","fathom core","fathom stone","je'neu sancrea","moonshrine ruins","twilight's hammer","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","topic:twilight-s-hammer","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},m={start="Je'neu Sancrea",level="27",faction="Horde",id=6921,ri={"Fathom Core"}},src={"Amongst the Ruins (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6922"] = {t="quest",n="Baron Aquanis",z="blackfathom",s="Beneath Ashenvale, Baron Aquanis leaves a strange globe filled with tainted fluid. Je'neu Sancrea of the Earthen Ring believes it may show what corrupted the elemental, and suspects the Twilight's Hammer cultists in the submerged ruins.",h="Beneath Ashenvale, Baron Aquanis leaves a strange globe filled with tainted fluid.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Heart",b="Blackfathom Deeps holds Baron Aquanis, a water spirit twisted by foul sorcery. When the elemental is destroyed, a Strange Water Globe remains behind. The impervious orb holds putrid fluid that seems to have sustained and warped Aquanis's natural essence. Physical force cannot harm it, and its energies unsettle those attuned to the balance of the elements.",sp=0},{t="Studies of the Earthen Ring",b="Je'neu Sancrea serves the Earthen Ring from a camp on the Zoram Strand. He recognizes the Strange Water Globe as evidence of unnatural meddling. The order suspects that dark forces corrupted Baron Aquanis, and Je'neu suspects the Twilight's Hammer cultists in the sunken temple. He studies the globe to test that suspicion and learn how the cultists subdue and twist Azeroth's elemental spirits.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Baron Aquanis?",a="Baron Aquanis is a powerful water elemental in the underground waters of Blackfathom Deeps. Dark practitioners in the ruined temple have corrupted and bound the elemental.",al={"who is aquanis","aquanis boss","baron aquanis lore"},it="target"},{q="What is the Strange Water Globe?",a="The Strange Water Globe is an impervious sphere left behind when Baron Aquanis is defeated. Putrid liquid sloshes inside, carrying the tainted energy that fueled the elemental's corrupted state.",al={"water globe","strange water globe","aquanis quest item"},it="item"},{q="Why does Je'neu Sancrea want the globe?",a="Je'neu Sancrea studies the globe to learn whether the Twilight's Hammer caused the corruption and to uncover the rites used to twist elemental spirits. As a member of the Earthen Ring, he watches for elemental disturbances across Ashenvale.",al={"why bring to jeneu","jeneu sancrea purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who is behind the corruption of Baron Aquanis?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cultists deep inside Blackfathom Deeps are the chief suspects. Their presence in the temple fits a pattern of desecration and dark communion with unnatural beings.",al={"who corrupted aquanis","aquanis twilight hammer","cultists blackfathom"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Je'neu Sancrea located?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is an Earthen Ring shaman camped along the Zoram Strand on Ashenvale's northwestern coast, near the entrance to the Blackfathom Deeps caverns.",al={"where is jeneu","turn in aquanis quest","where to turn in water globe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What follows the turn-in of this quest?",a="Handing over the globe leads to more inquiries into the region's elemental distress. Adventurers continue helping the Earthen Ring oppose the growing blight.",al={"next quest","elemental distress"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the Earthen Ring sees corruption of elemental spirits as a grave violation of the natural order. Investigating Baron Aquanis's tainted state is central to restoring elemental balance.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can join Je'neu Sancrea's work with Horde scouts at the Zoram'gar Outpost. They seek champions to cleanse the corrupted waters beneath Ashenvale's coast."},kw={"ashenvale","baron aquanis","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","elemental corruption","je'neu sancrea","strange water globe","twilight's hammer","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","zone:blackfathom","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},m={start="Strange Water Globe",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",level="30",faction="Horde",id=6922},src={"Baron Aquanis (quest)"}}
E["quest:824"] = {t="quest",n="Je'neu of the Earthen Ring",z="blackfathom",s="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Je'neu of the Earthen Ring studies a spreading corruption. Horde travelers bring him a corrupted water globe recovered from Ashenvale's elementals. As a shaman devoted to elemental harmony, he seeks to understand the blight along the Zoram Strand and within Blackfathom Deeps, in hope of halting the poison in the region's waters.",h="At Zoram'gar Outpost, Je'neu of the Earthen Ring studies a spreading corruption.",sec={{t="A Messenger for the Elements",b="Mastok Wrilehiss sends you to Je'neu Sancrea with a corrupted water globe recovered from Ashenvale's elementals. Strange elementals have surfaced across the region, animated by unnatural power that scouts cannot explain. Among their remains, the intact globe pulses with corrupted magic. Mastok knows soldiers and scouts lack the spiritual insight to understand it, so he directs Horde travelers to someone versed in ancient legends and elemental lore.",sp=0},{t="The Eyes of the Earthen Ring",b="Je'neu Sancrea serves the Earthen Ring, an order of shamans devoted to balance among Azeroth's primal forces. Horde forces guard the Zoram Strand frontier while he studies the spiritual wound in Blackfathom Deeps' nearby temple ruins. To Je'neu, an elemental drawing strength from a tainted vessel is no isolated threat. It is an alarming omen: unseen, ancient powers are perverting the natural order.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Je'neu Sancrea?",a="Je'neu Sancrea is a troll shaman of the Earthen Ring in northern Kalimdor. He devotes his life to communing with and studying the elements, and stays near the Zoram Strand to investigate dark disturbances rising from Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"who is jeneu","jeneu sancrea lore","what is jeneu doing here"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Earthen Ring?",a="The Earthen Ring is an order of shamans devoted to keeping Azeroth's primal elements in harmony. Its members study ancient lore, forgotten spirits, and old legends to mend elemental chaos and heal spiritual corruption across the world.",al={"what is earthen ring","who are earthen ring","earthen ring lore"},it="people"},{q="Where can Je'neu Sancrea be found?",a="Je'neu Sancrea can be found at Zoram'gar Outpost on the coast of the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale. There he studies elemental disturbances rising from nearby Blackfathom Deeps.",al={"where is jeneu","jeneu location","find jeneu sancrea"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Befouled Water Globe?",a="The Befouled Water Globe is a magical conduit through which powerful water elementals channel their strength. Its corrupted, intact state suggests dark forces are deliberately twisting and enslaving the local spirits.",al={"what is the globe","befouled globe lore","water globe"},it="item"},{q="Who sends you to speak with Je'neu?",a="Mastok Wrilehiss, a Horde officer stationed in Ashenvale, directs adventurers to deliver the tainted relic to Je'neu. The army cannot decipher its strange magical nature.",al={"who starts this quest","mastok quest"},it="origin"},{q="What will Je'neu do with the globe?",a="Je'neu takes custody of the vessel for the Earthen Ring to study its blight. He hopes that study will reveal how to cleanse the waters and restore peace to the region's troubled elementals.",al={"what happens to the globe","cure the corruption"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mastok Wrilehiss send you to Je'neu?",a="Mastok recognizes that the Befouled Water Globe is far beyond his expertise. Understanding corrupt magic, old legends, and disturbed elementals falls squarely into the realm of the Earthen Ring. He sends you to Je'neu Sancrea because Je'neu is a local shaman of the Ring who possesses the deep elemental knowledge needed to unravel the globe's true significance and threat.",al={"mastok wrilehiss motive","why send to jeneu","why does mastok want this done"},it="motive",add="5c718e13"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you help uphold elemental balance. Delivering the corrupted globe aids a fellow member of the Earthen Ring in diagnosing a dangerous spiritual sickness.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure the Ashenvale coastline by uncovering the dark origins of local elemental hostility near fortified camps such as Zoram'gar Outpost.",["race:Troll"]="As a troll, you can see Je'neu Sancrea's deep spiritual wisdom. He applies his ancestral bond with the spirits in service to the Earthen Ring."},kw={"befouled water globe","blackfathom deeps","earthen ring","elementals","je'neu sancrea","mastok wrilehiss","zoram strand","zoram'gar outpost"},rel={"npc:je-neu-sancrea","quest:1918","npc:mastok-wrilehiss","subzone:zoram-strand","subzone:zoram-gar-outpost","zone:blackfathom","zone:ashenvale","topic:old-god"},m={start="Mastok Wrilehiss",["end"]="Je'neu Sancrea",faction="Horde",id=824},src={"Je'neu of the Earthen Ring (quest)"}}
E["quest:971"] = {t="quest",n="Knowledge in the Deeps",z="blackfathom",s="In Ironforge, Gerrig Bonegrip sends you across the sea to seek an ancient manuscript. He wants the Lorgalis Manuscript from the sunken ruins of Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale.",h="In Ironforge, Gerrig Bonegrip sends you across the sea to seek an ancient manuscript.",sec={{t="A Scholar in the Shadows",b="In Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, Gerrig Bonegrip gathers ancient texts. His interests reach beyond ordinary histories and civic records. He seeks forgotten lore that can open doorways and awaken 'Those Who Sleep.'\n\nBonegrip speaks of surviving beyond 'the end days.' Such words make him seem either an eccentric scholar or a devotee of powers that slumber in shadow.",sp=0},{t="The Sunken Ruin of Lorgalis",b="Bonegrip sends you to Ashenvale's shadowed shores, where the night elven sanctuary of Blackfathom Deeps lies drowned. Before the Great Sundering tore Kalimdor apart, night elven scholars gathered great magical knowledge in coastal temples.\n\nNow naga, satyrs, and Twilight's Hammer cultists crawl through the flooded halls. Among them lies the Lorgalis Manuscript, forbidden lore kept in a Pitted Iron Chest.",sp=0},{t="Brothers and Sisters",b="When Gerrig Bonegrip receives the watersoaked manuscript, he does not take it to Ironforge's Hall of Explorers. He rejoices that copies will be made and shared with his mysterious 'brothers and sisters.'\n\nHe thanks the Alliance adventurer who recovered it, yet his loyalties lie with a hidden sect eager to use the lore in rites that could change the world. Bonegrip is tied to the Twilight's Hammer, whose followers seek forbidden knowledge of the Old Gods.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Knowledge in the Deeps?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip gives the request. He is a dwarf who seeks lore and lives in Forlorn Cavern, within Ironforge.",al={"quest giver","where to get quest","who starts knowledge in the deeps"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Lorgalis Manuscript?",a="The Lorgalis Manuscript is a text Gerrig Bonegrip wants recovered from Blackfathom Deeps. It lies in a Pitted Iron Chest among the flooded ruins.",al={"what is lorgalis manuscript","lorgalis lore","what book do i find"},it="item"},{q="Where is the Lorgalis Manuscript located?",a="The Lorgalis Manuscript lies deep inside Blackfathom Deeps, along the Zoram Strand on Ashenvale's northwestern coast in Kalimdor.",al={"lorgalis manuscript location","where is the book in bfd","bfd book location"},gp=true},{q="Who are 'Those Who Sleep' mentioned by Gerrig Bonegrip?",a="Bonegrip uses 'Those Who Sleep' for the slumbering powers described in the forbidden lore he collects.",al={"those who sleep","who is bonegrip talking about","what does gerrig worship"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the 'brothers and sisters' Gerrig plans to share the manuscript with?",a="Bonegrip's associates share his interest in forbidden lore. Recovering the manuscript can reveal more about whom he serves.",al={"gerrig brothers and sisters","who is gerrig working for","bonegrip faction"},sp=1,it="allies"},{q="Why does a quest in Ironforge send players all the way to Ashenvale?",a="Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern draws unsanctioned magic users, warlocks, and rogues seeking secrets hidden from the light. Bonegrip gathers old, powerful lore, and the Lorgalis Manuscript he seeks is said to lie beneath Blackfathom Deeps in Ashenvale, the old home of long-dead elves who held great knowledge.",al={"why go to ashenvale","ironforge to bfd quest","travel to blackfathom"},it="place"},{q="Why does Gerrig Bonegrip want the Lorgalis Manuscript?",a="Gerrig Bonegrip collects ancient, powerful texts capable of opening forgotten doorways and awakening Those Who Sleep. He believes the Lorgalis Manuscript holds long-lost secrets from the ancient night elves of Blackfathom Deeps, and he intends to copy and distribute its dark knowledge among his secretive brothers and sisters before the coming end days.",al={"gerrig bonegrip motive","why does gerrig want the manuscript","gerrig bonegrip quest reason"},sp=1,it="motive",add="32faf93b"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="In Ironforge's Forlorn Cavern, Bonegrip works alongside warlocks who hide there. He shares their hunger for forbidden texts that bend the planes.",["race:NightElf"]="The manuscript lies in Blackfathom Deeps, a drowned night elven sanctuary now occupied by cultists and other intruders.",["faction:Alliance"]="Helping an Alliance scholar seems harmless, but Bonegrip's motives and shadowy associates point to darker designs within Ironforge's walls."},kw={"ashenvale","blackfathom deeps","forlorn cavern","gerrig bonegrip","ironforge","knowledge in the deeps","lorgalis manuscript"},rel={"npc:gerrig-bonegrip","zone:blackfathom","subzone:forlorn-cavern","zone:ironforge","zone:ashenvale"},m={start="Gerrig Bonegrip",level="23",faction="Alliance",id=971,ri={"Lorgalis Manuscript"}},src={"Knowledge in the Deeps (Classic)"}}
E["subzone:aku-mai-s-lair"] = {t="subzone",n="Aku'mai's Lair",z="blackfathom",s="Beyond the Moonshrine Sanctum, Aku'mai's Lair lies beneath Blackfathom Deeps. In its flooded depths, cultists and naga gather around Aku'mai, a hydra they honor as a servant of the Old Gods.",h="Beyond the Moonshrine Sanctum, Aku'mai's Lair lies beneath Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Heart of the Depths",b="Four braziers flank a naga statue behind the Moonshrine Sanctum's sealed double doors. Lighting them awakens guardians sworn to defend the threshold. Beyond the doors, a sunless grotto lies beneath the water. Twilight's Hammer cultists and invading naga gather there in reverence of Aku'mai, an ancient, three-headed hydra they consider a living servant of the Old Gods.",sp=0},{t="Harbinger of Ruin",b="Twilight's Hammer cultists see Aku'mai as an omen of a promised age of darkness. They believe the beast's emergence and continued sustenance will herald the breaking of subterranean prisons holding their ancient deities. Sacrificial offerings feed Aku'mai, while dark magic guards the pool where it dwells. The cult's plans center on this beast as ancient evil claws its way back into Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Aku'mai's Lair located?",a="Aku'mai's Lair lies at the end of the Blackfathom Deeps cavern complex in Ashenvale, beyond the sealed doors of the Moonshrine Sanctum.",al={"where is akumai lair","how to get to akumai room","akumai lair location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you open the doors to Aku'mai's Lair?",a="Light the four ritual braziers around the naga statue in the Moonshrine Sanctum, then defeat the creatures summoned to guard them. The double doors into Aku'mai's Lair will open.",al={"open akumai door","how to unlock akumai lair","light fires akumai"},gp=true},{q="What dwells inside this cavern?",a="Aku'mai, a massive, three-headed hydra tainted by ancient dark powers, dwells in the cavern as a servant of the Old Gods.",al={"who is in akumai lair","what lives in akumai lair","boss in akumai lair"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Twilight's Hammer cult worshiping here?",a="Twilight's Hammer cultists revere Aku'mai as a servant of the Old Gods. They believe empowering the beast will help restore the age when the Old Gods ruled the world.",al={"why do cultists worship akumai","twilights hammer akumai lair","why is twilight hammer here"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Aku'mai's Lair?",a="Aku'mai's Lair is the deepest, darkest cavern within the submerged ruins of Blackfathom Deeps. Once part of an ancient night elven temple dedicated to Elune, this flooded hollow now serves as the sanctum for a monstrous three-headed hydra, a creature steeped in the malevolent influence of the Old Gods.",al={"what is akumais lair","akumai lair info","about akumais lair"},it="place",add="d1c19121"},{q="What happened to turn this place into Aku'mai's Lair?",a="Following the ancient Great Sundering, the temple of Blackfathom sank beneath the tides and fell into forgotten ruin. Over the centuries, corruption seeped into its flooded underbelly, allowing the dread hydra Aku'mai to claim these submerged chambers as a nest while dark cultists and naga gathered to venerate it.",al={"akumais lair history","what happened at akumais lair","how did akumais lair form"},it="history",add="b75b148a"},{q="Is Aku'mai's Lair dangerous?",a="It is extraordinarily perilous. Beyond the gauntlet of zealots and naga guarding the Moonshrine Sanctum, the lair itself houses a colossal servant of the Old Gods. Aku'mai lashes out with caustic breath, crushing fury, and primordial malice capable of tearing apart unprepared adventurers.",al={"is akumais lair dangerous","how dangerous is akumais lair","danger akumais lair"},it="danger",add="7d86eb37"},{q="Why is this cavern called Aku'mai's Lair?",a="The cavern takes its name from its monstrous inhabitant, Aku'mai. The massive, corrupted hydra has dwelt here long enough to claim the hollow as its personal nesting ground, revered by the Twilight's Hammer and naga who wait upon its dark awakening.",al={"why is it called akumais lair","akumais lair name meaning","who named akumais lair"},it="name",add="39ca825a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see a desecrated temple of Elune turned into a foul nest for an Old God spawn. Such defilement of Ashenvale's sacred soil is intolerable.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see Aku'mai's watery den as a severe blight on Kalimdor's waterways and beasts. Its vile mutation and unnatural corruption spread through the depths."},kw={"aku'mai's lair","akumai","blackfathom deeps","hydra","moonshrine sanctum","naga","old gods","twilight's hammer"},rel={"npc:aku-mai","zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-sanctum","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:old-god","topic:naga"},src={"Aku'mai's Lair"}}
E["subzone:drowned-sacellum"] = {t="subzone",n="Drowned Sacellum",z="blackfathom",s="At Blackfathom Deeps' entrance, the Drowned Sacellum lies submerged beneath the coast. Brackish saltwater and cavern roots surround its broken stones, now occupied by murlocs and makrura.",h="At Blackfathom Deeps' entrance, the Drowned Sacellum lies submerged beneath the coast.",sec={{t="A Submerged Sanctuary",b="You enter the Drowned Sacellum just beyond Blackfathom Deeps' threshold. The chapel once offered quiet worship to Elune, but it has long since collapsed into the sea-swept abyss beneath Ashenvale's coast. Brackish pools swallow its ancient marble flagstones, where starfish cling beneath the cavern ceiling's massive roots. Dark wisps flicker dimly through the gloom, lighting a broken stone path. Careful steps along it lead deeper into the temple complex, toward the Pool of Ask'ar.",sp=0},{t="Den of Scavengers",b="Night elf caretakers left the Drowned Sacellum long ago, and shoreline scavengers now hold the ruins. Packs of aggressive murlocs and heavily armored makrura share the murky waters and attack anyone who disturbs their nesting grounds. Darker cultic threats lie deeper in the temple, but these predators guard the first stretch of the underground ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Drowned Sacellum originally used for?",a="A sacellum is a small roofless shrine or chapel. Before the Sundering, this one served as an elven place of worship to Elune within the greater subterranean temple complex.",al={"drowned sacellum purpose","what is the drowned sacellum","sacellum history"},it="purpose"},{q="What creatures inhabit this part of the caverns?",a="Wild murlocs and makrura occupy the flooded ruins. They thrive in the brackish pools and nesting crevices.",al={"drowned sacellum mobs","what lives in drowned sacellum","monsters in drowned sacellum"},it="residents"},{q="How do you navigate past the Drowned Sacellum?",a="Carefully cross the crumbling, half-submerged platforms and pillars rising out of the water to reach the tunnel ahead, which leads to the Pool of Ask'ar.",al={"how to get through drowned sacellum","drowned sacellum jump","path to pool of askar"},gp=true},{q="Where does the light in the cavern come from?",a="Dark wisps floating among thick, twisted tree roots that pierce the ceiling from the Ashenvale forests above provide the cavern's faint, eerie light.",al={"why is it glowing","wisps in drowned sacellum","drowned sacellum lighting"}},{q="What is the Drowned Sacellum?",a="The Drowned Sacellum is a ruined, subterranean shrine located just inside the entrance of the Blackfathom Deeps caverns. Lying half-submerged in a pool of dark saltwater, its ancient stonework is now crusted over with starfish and choked by the thick tree roots hanging from the cavern ceiling above.",al={"what is drowned sacellum","drowned sacellum lore","drowned sacellum blackfathom"},it="place",add="b0803046"},{q="Why is it called the Drowned Sacellum?",a="A sacellum is a small, consecrated shrine or chapel. This particular sanctuary earned its grim moniker because the surrounding ocean waters have seeped into the subterranean caverns, completely flooding its chambers and leaving its sacred altar partially submerged under saltwater.",al={"why drowned sacellum","drowned sacellum name meaning","sacellum name origin"},it="name",add="515e8f31"},{q="Is the Drowned Sacellum dangerous?",a="Yes. Though it was once a sacred place of worship, the drowned shrine is now infested by aggressive murlocs and armored makrura. They dwell together among the murky pools and ruined pillars, viciously attacking anyone attempting to delve deeper into the Blackfathom caverns.",al={"is drowned sacellum safe","drowned sacellum threats","danger drowned sacellum"},it="danger",add="97f28086"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, this ancient shrine's submersion in saltwater and its occupation by murlocs recall the Kaldorei heritage lost beneath the Zoram Strand.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see massive tree roots piercing the stone ceiling from the surface above, proof that nature endures amid the corrupted underground waters."},kw={"bfd","blackfathom deeps","drowned sacellum","makrura","murloc","shrine","zoram strand"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","topic:murloc"},src={"Drowned Sacellum"}}
E["subzone:forgotten-pool"] = {t="subzone",n="Forgotten Pool",z="blackfathom",s="Past the Moonshrine Ruins, Forgotten Pool lies beneath the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps. Its dark waters hide monstrous deep-sea predators.",h="Past the Moonshrine Ruins, Forgotten Pool lies beneath the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="A Submerged Lair",b="You reach Forgotten Pool by diving through the sunken waterways beyond the Moonshrine Ruins. Dark water fills this isolated cavern, cut off from dry ground. Twilight's Hammer cultists chant nearby, and naga patrol the flooded halls, but the pool lies apart from them. Old Serra'kis, an ancient aquatic terror, lairs in its depths, hidden by the water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Forgotten Pool located?",a="Forgotten Pool lies deep within Blackfathom Deeps, beyond the Moonshrine Ruins. You reach the submerged cavern by swimming through flooded tunnels.",al={"where is forgotten pool","forgotten pool location","how to find forgotten pool"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What lurks inside the Forgotten Pool?",a="Old Serra'kis, an ancient thresher-like beast of the deep waters, lurks in Forgotten Pool. The secluded cavern is its lair.",al={"forgotten pool monster","who lives in forgotten pool","forgotten pool boss"},it="threat"},{q="Does the Forgotten Pool lead anywhere else?",a="No. Forgotten Pool is an underwater dead end with no further passageways. It is a secluded aquatic nest.",al={"is forgotten pool a dead end","where does forgotten pool go"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Forgotten Pool?",a="The Forgotten Pool is a flooded subterranean cavern tucked away in the depths of Blackfathom Deeps, just beyond the Moonshrine Ruins. Cut off from the temple corridors by submerged passages, it forms a stagnant, secluded aquatic dead-end deep beneath the ruins of the ancient night elven sanctuary.",al={"what is forgotten pool","forgotten pool lore","about forgotten pool"},it="place",add="5f3c8292"},{q="Is the Forgotten Pool dangerous?",a="Yes, swimming through its dark, waterlogged tunnels presents severe perils. Beyond the risk of drowning in the submerged passages, the pool serves as the lair of Old Serra'kis, a monstrous aquatic thresher, alongside other lurking horrors that make diving into its depths perilous for any unwary explorer.",al={"is forgotten pool dangerous","danger forgotten pool","forgotten pool threats"},it="danger",add="a4c2428d"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde scout in Blackfathom Deeps, you may find Old Serra'kis lurking in Forgotten Pool, far from the cult's chanting halls."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","cavern","forgotten pool","moonshrine ruins","old serra'kis","thresher","underwater"},rel={"npc:old-serra-kis","zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","zone:ashenvale","topic:horde"},src={"Forgotten Pool"}}
E["subzone:moonshrine-ruins"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonshrine Ruins",z="blackfathom",s="Deep in Blackfathom Deeps, the Moonshrine Ruins lie flooded and seized by the Twilight's Hammer. Their halls once honored Elune, but the cult now carries out dark rituals among the ancient stones.",h="Deep in Blackfathom Deeps, the Moonshrine Ruins lie flooded and seized by the Twilight's Hammer.",sec={{t="Flooded Halls of Elune",b="Beyond the cavernous Pool of Ask'ar, the Moonshrine Ruins lie along the Ashenvale coast. These partly submerged halls once echoed with chants to Elune, the Moon Goddess. The Great Sundering shattered the temple and drowned its lower levels in seawater. Now murky waters churn with aggressive crabs and serpentine threshadons. The Twilight's Hammer cult holds the stones and performs dark rituals that mock the shrine's sacred origins.",sp=0},{t="The Elemental Depths",b="The flooded ruins connect toward the Forgotten Pool and Moonshrine Sanctum. Beneath their waters rests an ancient runestone bound to the elements. Through it, the Twilight's Hammer manipulates the deeps and calls forth Baron Aquanis, a monstrous water elemental bound to the cult's dark designs.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What were the Moonshrine Ruins originally built for?",a="The Moonshrine Ruins were part of a grand underground temple complex dedicated to Elune, the night elven goddess. The temple was built before the Great Sundering tore the ancient continent apart.",al={"moonshrine origins","who built moonshrine ruins","what is this place"},it="origin"},{q="Who controls the Moonshrine Ruins now?",a="The Twilight's Hammer cultists and hostile aquatic beasts, including threshadons and snapping crabs, have overrun the sunken complex.",al={"who is here","moonshrine mobs","twilights hammer blackfathom"},it="residents"},{q="Where do the Moonshrine Ruins lead?",a="The Moonshrine Ruins lie beyond the tunnels past the Pool of Ask'ar. Their paths lead deeper toward Moonshrine Sanctum and provide access to the Forgotten Pool.",al={"moonshrine exits","where does this go","path through ruins"},it="place"},{q="Who is Baron Aquanis?",a="Baron Aquanis is a powerful water elemental summoned through a submerged runestone hidden beneath the ruins. The Twilight's Hammer uses him to serve its dark aims.",al={"baron aquanis lore","underwater boss moonshrine","elemental in water"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Moonshrine Ruins?",a="The Moonshrine Ruins are a sunken cavern complex situated deep within Blackfathom Deeps. Once an ancient night elven sanctuary dedicated to Elune, the halls are now partially submerged beneath subterranean waters. Corrupted cultists and feral aquatic predators prowl through the ruined arches and flooded chambers.",al={"what is moonshrine ruins","moonshrine ruins lore","about moonshrine ruins"},it="place",add="b0a2ccc3"},{q="Why is the Moonshrine Ruins so dangerous?",a="The ruins harbor both fanatical Twilight's Hammer cultists and vicious aquatic wildlife. Swarming crabs and massive threshadons churn through the flooded pathways, ready to drag swimmers down, while cultists conduct dark rituals in the shadows.",al={"is moonshrine ruins dangerous","moonshrine ruins danger","threats in moonshrine ruins"},it="danger",add="e8d3a9e3"},{q="Why is it called the Moonshrine Ruins?",a="The chamber draws its name from the ancient night elven shrines that originally honored the moon goddess, Elune. Following the Sundering and centuries of neglect, those once-glorious holy places collapsed into the flooded, broken stones you see today.",al={"why is it called moonshrine ruins","moonshrine ruins name","moonshrine meaning"},it="name",add="9bba1602"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For a night elf, seeing these sacred halls to Elune flooded and overrun by the cult is a bitter grievance.",["class:Shaman"]="For a shaman, the runestone that binds Baron Aquanis shows how the Twilight's Hammer distorts and enslaves elemental forces."},kw={"aquanis","blackfathom","moonshrine","ruins","sanctum","threshadon","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","subzone:moonshrine-sanctum","quest:6922","subzone:pool-of-ask-ar","subzone:forgotten-pool","topic:twilight-s-hammer"},src={"Moonshrine Ruins"}}
E["subzone:moonshrine-sanctum"] = {t="subzone",n="Moonshrine Sanctum",z="blackfathom",s="Within Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight's Hammer gathers beneath Queen Azshara's statue. Twilight Lord Kelris watches over the ancient shrine, which guards the sealed way to Aku'mai's lair.",h="Within Blackfathom Deeps, Twilight's Hammer gathers beneath Queen Azshara's statue.",sec={{t="A Desecrated Temple",b="Past the flooded Moonshrine Ruins, cultists gather in the Moonshrine Sanctum, the heart of Twilight's Hammer activity inside Blackfathom Deeps. Night elves built the hall millennia ago to honor the moon and their rulers. Now the cult has defiled it, yet carefully maintains the towering statue of Queen Azshara. Beneath the cavernous stone ceiling, Twilight Lord Kelris watches as the cultists chant dark rituals day and night.",sp=0},{t="The Threshold to Aku'mai",b="The sanctum's heavy double stone doors seal Aku'mai's Lair behind ancient wards. Four ritual braziers stand around Azshara's statue; lighting them breaks the seal. The flames also rouse the shrine's guardians: giant crabs, snapped-jaw turtles, armored makrura, and conjured water elementals, all bound to defend the sanctum from intruders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Moonshrine Sanctum?",a="Moonshrine Sanctum lies deep inside Blackfathom Deeps, along the Zoram Strand in Ashenvale. Past the flooded Moonshrine Ruins, it stands just before the lair of Aku'mai the hydra.",al={"moonshrine sanctum location","where is moonshrine sanctum","bfd sanctum"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who rules over the Moonshrine Sanctum?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris commands the sanctum. A formidable sorcerer who weaves sleep, he leads Twilight's Hammer rituals in honor of its ancient patron, touched by the void.",al={"who leads here","boss of moonshrine sanctum","who runs the sanctum"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is there an intact statue of Azshara here?",a="Night elves built the sanctum as an ancient temple dedicated to Queen Azshara before the Great Sundering. Twilight's Hammer keeps her statue in good condition and seems to have no quarrel with the queen it honors.",al={"azshara statue","why statue of azshara","naga statue bfd"},it="origin"},{q="How do you open the large doors at the back of the chamber?",a="Ignite the four ritual candles around the feet of Azshara's statue to open the doors to Aku'mai's Lair. Each flame awakens waves of guardian aquatic beasts and water elementals that must be subdued.",al={"how to open bfd doors","akumai door open","light candles bfd"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Moonshrine Sanctum?",a="The Moonshrine Sanctum is an ancient temple chamber deep within the Blackfathom Deeps. Once devoted to Queen Azshara, it now serves as the inner seat of power for the local Twilight's Hammer cult, who conduct dark rituals in the presence of an intact monument to the naga queen.",al={"what is moonshrine sanctum","moonshrine sanctum info","about moonshrine sanctum"},it="place",add="6ea53622"},{q="What happened to the Moonshrine Sanctum?",a="Originally built as an ancient elven shrine dedicated to Queen Azshara, the sanctum survived the Great Sundering beneath the waters of Ashenvale. In recent times, the Twilight's Hammer cult discovered the subterranean temple and claimed it as their high seat, repurposing its ancient halls to perform dark rites.",al={"moonshrine sanctum history","what happened at moonshrine sanctum","history of moonshrine sanctum"},it="history",add="67d36571"},{q="Is the Moonshrine Sanctum dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The chamber is heavily guarded by fanatical Twilight's Hammer cultists led by Twilight Lord Kelris. Furthermore, the shrine itself is warded by dangerous guardians, and it lies right before the threshold to Aku'mai's lair.",al={"how dangerous is moonshrine sanctum","is moonshrine sanctum safe","dangers of moonshrine sanctum"},it="danger",add="99e9f82b"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see an ancient temple carved by your ancestors before the Sundering, now turned into a sacrificial hollow for Twilight's Hammer and naga. Ashenvale's shadows reach even here.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you hear Twilight Lord Kelris's twisted rituals turn sacred devotion toward maddening whispers of the void, far from restorative divine prayer."},kw={"aku'mai","azshara","blackfathom","candles","kelris","moonshrine","sanctum","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","subzone:aku-mai-s-lair","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","npc:aku-mai","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:naga"},src={"Moonshrine Sanctum"}}
E["subzone:pool-of-ask-ar"] = {t="subzone",n="Pool of Ask'ar",z="blackfathom",s="Naga invaders and aquatic beasts crowd the Pool of Ask'ar, deep within Blackfathom Deeps. Its submerged halls hold night elven stonework and passages into the corrupted sanctuary.",h="Naga invaders and aquatic beasts crowd the Pool of Ask'ar, deep within Blackfathom Deeps.",sec={{t="Depths of the Sunken Grotto",b="Past the Drowned Sacellum, cold, murky water fills the Pool of Ask'ar beneath a vast cavern vault. Oversized snapping turtles and deep-sea crabs nest among natural caverns and ancient stonework, watched over by Ghamoo-ra, an enormous ancient chelonian. Naga have seized the temple and use this flooded threshold to guard the approaches leading deeper into the complex, toward Lady Sarevess and the Moonshrine Ruins.",sp=0},{t="Secrets Beneath the Surface",b="The Pool of Ask'ar hides relics from the shrine's past before the Sundering, beyond its dangerous creatures and naga patrols. Submerged ledges and hidden alcoves along the cavern's edges hold lost artifacts, including the Lorgalis Manuscript sought by Gerrig Bonegrip, a dwarven scholar from Ironforge. Swim through the flooded southern passages to reach dry tunnels guarded by vile murlocs and Old God cultists. The pool remains a vital waterway through Blackfathom Deeps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Pool of Ask'ar?",a="Past the Drowned Sacellum, the vast Pool of Ask'ar lies deep within Blackfathom Deeps. Snapping turtles, crabs, and naga guards crowd its waters.",al={"pool of askar","what is this pool","bfd water area"},it="place"},{q="Who lives in this subterranean pool?",a="Snapping turtles and crabs inhabit the cavern, with Ghamoo-ra, a colossal turtle, among them. Hostile naga patrol the submerged banks and nearby chambers.",al={"pool monsters","pool of askar bosses","who is in the pool"},it="residents"},{q="Where do the underwater tunnels lead?",a="The flooded southern passages lead toward chambers occupied by Lady Sarevess and Argent Guard Thaelrid. They also open onto a route past Gelihast toward the Moonshrine Ruins.",al={"pool tunnels","where does the water go","pool of askar exit"},gp=true},{q="What notable items can be found in the pool?",a="The submerged ruins around the pool hold the Lorgalis Manuscript, an ancient text on the Old Gods sought by Gerrig Bonegrip of Ironforge.",al={"pool of askar relics","lorgalis manuscript","pool loot"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is the Pool of Ask'ar dangerous?",a="Venturing into this flooded cavern poses severe danger. Hostile naga patrol the surrounding ruins and passages, while aggressive subterranean crabs and snapjaws infest the dark waters. Even deeper beneath the surface, ancient and colossal beasts lurk, ready to drag unwary swimmers into the suffocating depths.",al={"is pool of ask'ar dangerous","pool of askar danger","threats in pool of askar"},it="danger",add="87a1a296"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, the pool drowns grounds once holy to Elune, submerging ancient architecture and leaving sacred relics such as the Lorgalis Manuscript for naga to scavenge.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you must breach the waterways to uncover Argent Guard Thaelrid's fate. He entered these depths on a holy mission against the Twilight's Hammer."},kw={"blackfathom deeps","drowned sacellum","ghamoo-ra","lady sarevess","lorgalis manuscript","naga","pool of ask'ar"},rel={"zone:blackfathom","npc:ghamoo-ra-classic","subzone:drowned-sacellum","npc:lady-sarevess","subzone:moonshrine-ruins","topic:naga","npc:gelihast","npc:lorgus-jett"},src={"Pool of Ask'ar"}}
E["zone:blackfathom"] = {t="dungeon",n="Blackfathom Deeps",z="blackfathom",s="Twilight's Hammer cultists now gather in the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps, along the Zoram Strand in northwestern Ashenvale. The temple once honored Elune, the night elven moon goddess. Naga and satyrs have joined the cult in veneration of Aku'mai, a primordial hydra and servant of an Old God.",h="Twilight's Hammer cultists now gather in the flooded halls of Blackfathom Deeps, along the Zoram Strand in...",sec={{t="Sunken Sanctum of Elune",b="Blackfathom Deeps once honored Elune, the night elven moon goddess. Long before the Great Sundering shattered ancient Kalimdor, Highborne masons raised gem-encrusted bridges through its splendid halls. Queen Azshara commanded the waters around the sacred moonwell, keeping salt seas and mountain streams apart. When the Sundering broke the world ten thousand years ago, the temple sank beneath the coastal waters of the Veiled Sea. It lay undisturbed for millennia, until foul whispers began to rise from the darkness below.",sp=0},{t="A Den of Ancient Horrors",b="Twilight's Hammer cultists came to the sunken ruins, drawn by mad dreams and dark portents. Inside, they forged an unholy truce with coastal naga led by Lady Sarevess and prowling satyrs. Together, they desecrated the moonwell and enslaved the creatures nearby. Years of torment drove the giant sea turtle Ghamoo-ra mad. The brutal murloc Gelihast raised a blood shrine, and the caverns filled with fresh sacrifices. Under Twilight Lord Kelris, the cultists made the ruins a staging ground for the Old Gods' impending return.",sp=0},{t="The Beast in the Deep",b="Aku'mai dwells in the deepest heart of the sunken temple. The ancient three-headed hydra serves an Old God and rose from the waters after its corruption tainted the temple's Moon Well. Twilight Lord Kelris and his cultists sacrifice innocents to Aku'mai for power. Striking down Kelris and lighting the ritual candles in his sanctum opens the way to the beast's lair, where champions can slay Aku'mai before its evil spreads across Kalimdor.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Blackfathom Deeps before it fell into darkness?",a="Blackfathom Deeps began as a magnificent night elven temple devoted to Elune, the moon goddess. Crystal-clear pools, gemmed bridges, and a blessed moonwell filled its halls, under Queen Azshara's watch, until the Great Sundering broke the temple and sank it beneath the sea.",al={"bfd history","who built bfd","original temple"},it="history"},{q="Why are the Twilight's Hammer cultists here?",a="Nightmare visions and whispering voices from beneath Azeroth drew the cultists to worship the Old Gods. Under Twilight Lord Kelris, they seized the sunken ruins and nurture Aku'mai with living sacrifices, hoping to hasten their chaotic masters' return.",al={"cultists in bfd","why is twilight's hammer here","what do cultists want"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Twilight Lord Kelris?",a="Twilight Lord Kelris leads the Twilight's Hammer cell in Blackfathom Deeps. He seeks the return of the Old Gods, directs the cult's sacrifices to Aku'mai, and oversees the temple's desecration.",al={"who is kelris","kelris lore","leader of bfd"},it="identity"},{q="What are the naga and satyr doing in the ruins?",a="Naga and satyrs were drawn to the drowned temple by lingering ancient magical energies. Led by Lady Sarevess, the naga made a pact with the Twilight's Hammer: the cultists provide captives and dark knowledge, while her sea witches shield them from horrors in the deep.",al={"why are naga here","why satyrs in bfd","lady sarevess"},it="residents"},{q="Why do the Earthen Ring and Argent Dawn care about this place?",a="The Argent Dawn sent Scout Thaelrid to investigate suspected alliances between the naga and cultists, and he uncovered proof of their murderous rituals. The Earthen Ring rushed to Ashenvale because invoking the Old Gods threatens elemental balance and the world's safety.",al={"earthen ring ashenvale","argent dawn bfd","scout thaelrid"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when Aku'mai is defeated?",a="Slaying Aku'mai cuts off the Old Gods' immediate physical foothold in Ashenvale. It ends the cult's hope of restoring their reign through the ancient hydra, deals a major blow to the Twilight's Hammer, and cleanses part of the dark taint infecting the ruined moonwell.",al={"what happens when you kill aku'mai","aku'mai ending","after killing final boss"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Blackfathom Deeps is a sprawling, partially submerged subterranean cavern complex situated beneath the Zoram Strand along northwestern Ashenvale. Once an ancient night elven sanctuary, its flooded passages and marble halls have been overrun by vile forces. Today, it serves as a corrupted subterranean stronghold where dark cultists, serpent naga, and twisted aquatic beasts gather around a shrine devoted to the chaotic Old Gods.",al={"what is bfd","what is blackfathom","about blackfathom deeps"},it="place",add="45e74127",nx={8}},{q="Why is Blackfathom Deeps underwater?",a="Ten thousand years ago, the catastrophic Great Sundering tore ancient Kalimdor apart and shattered the surrounding coastline. The temple complex sank beneath the waters of the Veiled Sea as the land gave way. Over the millennia, the ocean swallowed most of its lower halls and courtyards, turning its majestic promenades into a flooded network of subterranean caves and tidal grottos.",al={"why is it flooded","why underwater bfd","how did it sink"},it="ruin",add="0e7de610"},{q="Who is Aku'Mai?",a="Aku'mai is a monstrous, ancient three-headed hydra and a servant of an Old God. When the Old God's corruption seeped up from beneath the earth and tainted the temple's sacred Moon Well, Aku'mai rose from the waters, and it now lurks in the deepest cavern of the ruins. The Twilight's Hammer worships the beast and sacrifices innocents to it for power.",al={"who is akumai","what is akumai","hydra boss bfd"},it="threat",add="55d79134",nx={10,11}},{q="Is Aku'Mai still alive down there?",a="Yes. Aku'mai dwells alive within its subterranean lair at the heart of the ruins. The Twilight's Hammer cultists guard the monstrous hydra and sacrifice captured innocents to it in exchange for dark power.",al={"is akumai alive","is akumai asleep","is akumai still down there"},it="danger",add="10cbfa4e"},{q="Who worships Aku'Mai?",a="Aku'mai is worshipped by the fanatical Twilight's Hammer cult, led within the ruins by Twilight Lord Kelris. They revere the hydra as a servant of their dark masters and believe that empowering it will help bring back the era when the Old Gods ruled the world.",al={"who worships akumai","akumai worshippers","cultists worshipping akumai"},it="people",add="cc477b61"},{q="Why does everyone seem so worried about this place?",a="Whenever the Old Gods are invoked, grave danger threatens all of Azeroth. Outside factions like the Argent Dawn and the Earthen Ring recognize that the gathering of cultists, naga, and satyrs under one dark banner portends catastrophic chaos. The cult's rituals, sacrifices, and worship of Aku'mai corrupt the surrounding waters and threaten to spread madness across Ashenvale.",al={"why worry bfd","why is blackfathom dangerous","threat of blackfathom"},it="threat",add="e60c1e85"},{q="Why are there naga and murlocs in the same ruins?",a="Both were drawn by the dark energies awakening within the ruins. The naga emerged from the sea to plumb the ancient power of the shattered temple and struck a sinister pact with the cult. Meanwhile, the murloc warrior Gelihast answered the call of the Old Gods, carving his way in and earning the cult's respect through raw brutality.",al={"why naga and murlocs","murlocs in bfd","naga in bfd"},it="threat",add="b8724226"},{q="Why me? Why send a stranger in instead of an army?",a="Marching an army into the sunken, flooded caverns is a logistical nightmare, and factions like the Argent Dawn operate quietly through scouts to avoid alerting the cult. Their covert scout, Thaelrid, was ambushed and mortally wounded within the halls. With time running out, they rely on capable, discreet champions like you to strike Kelris down before the cult's plans bear fruit.",al={"why send adventurers","why not send an army","why me bfd"},it="why_me",add="cd1d34a5"},{q="If I kill Kelris, what happens next?",a="Kelris's death does not immediately clear the caverns. Defeating him leaves behind four ceremonial altar candles in his sanctum. Lighting these candles breaks the seals holding back the sanctuary's dark wards, triggering waves of cult defenders and opening the massive stone doorway that leads directly into Aku'mai's inner lair.",al={"after kelris is dead","kill kelris what happens","what happens when kelris dies"},sp=1,it="next_step",add="f5e67a9b"},{q="How did I end up in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="You followed rumors of ancient darkness to the misty Zoram Strand in northwestern Ashenvale. Hidden among the shoreline's ruins, a stair-lined shaft drops into the earth, forcing you to dive through flooded tunnels to reach these drowned halls. Whether dispatched by the night elves of Darnassus to find missing scouts, guided by the shaman of the Earthen Ring to investigate rising elemental corruption, or chasing whispers of the cultists amassing beneath the surf, your path led directly into the submerged sanctuary.",al={"how did i get here","how do i get in here","how did i find this place"},it="arrival",add="f0f9473c"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Blackfathom Deeps?",a="You are here to purge the ancient temple of the evils festering within. The Twilight's Hammer cult, guided by Twilight Lord Kelris, has joined forces with local naga and satyrs to worship and feed the primordial beast Aku'mai. To stop their grim rituals, you must strike down the cultist leadership, put an end to the naga sorcery poisoning the waters, and venture into the lowest sanctum to slay the monstrous hydra before the servant of the Old Gods can unleash chaos upon Azeroth.",al={"what am i doing here","why am i here","what is my goal here","what is my mission here"},it="purpose",add="39220d00"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see a beloved part of your heritage desecrated: an ancient shrine of Elune and its sacred moonwell befouled by void cultists and monstrous aberrations.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman answering Je'neu and the Earthen Ring, you must plunge into the watery dark to halt the corruption of the elements and banish the Old Gods' chaotic taint.",["faction:Horde"]="From Zoram'gar Outpost, the Horde seeks to secure Ashenvale's northern coast against naga aggression and keep the dark rituals from threatening its outposts.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you enter to rescue Scout Thaelrid, recover lost Highborne knowledge, and help the night elves cleanse their sacred homeland of cultist terror."},kw={"aku'mai","bfd","blackfathom","deeps","gelihast","ghamoo-ra","kelris","sarevess","zoram"},rel={"npc:aku-mai","npc:twilight-lord-kelris","npc:lady-sarevess","npc:scout-thaelrid","quest:1200","quest:1199","quest:824","subzone:zoram-strand"},m={levels="24-32"},src={"Blackfathom Deeps (Classic)","Blackfathom Deeps"}}
